msgstr "A simple concrete wall, painted grey."

msgid "A glass window with a heavy makeshift shutter bolted into the window frame, with a wooden bar to close it from the inside.  The shutters are currently open, and offer no more defense than any glass window."
msgstr "A glass window with a heavy makeshift shutter bolted into the window frame, with a wooden bar to close it from the inside.  The shutters are currently open, and offer no more defence than any glass window."

msgid "A glass window with a heavy makeshift shutter bolted into the window frame, with a wooden bar to close it from the inside.  Both the shutters and the window glass are wide open, offering no defense."
msgstr "A glass window with a heavy makeshift shutter bolted into the window frame, with a wooden bar to close it from the inside.  Both the shutters and the window glass are wide open, offering no defence."

msgid "armored boarded up window"
msgstr "armoured boarded up window"

msgid "A giant sheet of glass inserted into a window with thick security grilles, making it impossible to crawl through.  Typically installed in high-value stores, or ones in bad neighborhoods."
msgstr "A giant sheet of glass inserted into a window with thick security grilles, making it impossible to crawl through.  Typically installed in high-value stores, or ones in bad neighbourhoods."

msgid "A window frame blocked with thick security grilles, making it impossible to crawl through.  Typically installed in high-value stores, or ones in bad neighborhoods."
msgstr "A window frame blocked with thick security grilles, making it impossible to crawl through.  Typically installed in high-value stores, or ones in bad neighbourhoods."

msgid "A giant sheet of glass inserted into a window with thick security grilles, making it impossible to crawl through.  Typically installed in high-value stores, or ones in bad neighborhoods.  It has a small sticker in one corner, reading 'Protected by SecuriCorp.  Keeping you safe since 1993.'"
msgstr "A giant sheet of glass inserted into a window with thick security grilles, making it impossible to crawl through.  Typically installed in high-value stores, or ones in bad neighbourhoods.  It has a small sticker in one corner, reading 'Protected by SecuriCorp.  Keeping you safe since 1993.'"

msgid "A giant sheet of glass inserted into a window with thick security grilles, making it impossible to crawl through.  Typically installed in high-value stores, or ones in bad neighborhoods.  This one has been retrofitted with curtains, which are currently open."
msgstr "A giant sheet of glass inserted into a window with thick security grilles, making it impossible to crawl through.  Typically installed in high-value stores, or ones in bad neighbourhoods.  This one has been retrofitted with curtains, which are currently open."

msgid "black fiberglass fence"
msgstr "black fibreglass fence"

msgid "A pile of glass ground so finely that the slightest breeze bears it aloft into mesmerizing clouds."
msgstr "A pile of glass ground so finely that the slightest breeze bears it aloft into mesmerising clouds."

msgid "You see a beautiful pillar the color of roses or blood, absolutely perfect in its proportions.  As your eyes are drawn to it, you feel a burning sensation on your skin.  You have learned the Laughing Man Passcode."
msgstr "You see a beautiful pillar the colour of roses or blood, absolutely perfect in its proportions.  As your eyes are drawn to it, you feel a burning sensation on your skin.  You have learned the Laughing Man Passcode."

msgid "You see a beautiful pillar the color of roses or blood, absolutely perfect in its proportions.  As your eyes are drawn to it, you feel a burning sensation on your skin.  <ls_obelisk_firsttime1> a tattoo of a handsome man laughing.  At first glance it appears charming and friendly, but the longer you examine it, the more it appears to be inhumanly cold and cruel; it's the 'Laughing Man Passcode'.  <ls_obelisk_firsttime2>"
msgstr "You see a beautiful pillar the colour of roses or blood, absolutely perfect in its proportions.  As your eyes are drawn to it, you feel a burning sensation on your skin.  <ls_obelisk_firsttime1> a tattoo of a handsome man laughing.  At first glance it appears charming and friendly, but the longer you examine it, the more it appears to be inhumanly cold and cruel; it's the 'Laughing Man Passcode'.  <ls_obelisk_firsttime2>"

msgid "A section of flooring made out of a tough, smooth material, colored in an atrocious mottled brown."
msgstr "A section of flooring made out of a tough, smooth material, coloured in an atrocious mottled brown."

msgid "A simple wall paneled in a coarsely textured gray laminate of some sort."
msgstr "A simple wall panelled in a coarsely textured grey laminate of some sort."

msgid "A gray textured door, rimmed in chrome, like a very tacky version of a ship's hatch."
msgstr "A grey textured door, rimmed in chrome, like a very tacky version of a ship's hatch."

msgid "waterlogged windshield"
msgstr "waterlogged windscreen"

msgid "Paint that comes in a sealed, pressurized container and is released in an aerosol spray when a valve button is depressed."
msgstr "Paint that comes in a sealed, pressurised container and is released in an aerosol spray when a valve button is depressed."

msgid "Ink comprised of a main carrier solvent, a glyceride, a pyrrolidone, a resin, and a colorant, making it water resistant."
msgstr "Ink comprised of a main carrier solvent, a glyceride, a pyrrolidone, a resin, and a colourant, making it water resistant."

msgid "Harness the power of radiation in your own home!  It looks similar to a D-cell battery, but actually contains folded layers of radioactive material inside.  It can produce electricity for several years at a steady voltage… but it's barely enough to power a small LED, and these batteries were worth hundreds of dollars.  Mostly they're a good way to brag to your neighbors that you have a nuclear power source in your house."
msgstr "Harness the power of radiation in your own home!  It looks similar to a D-cell battery, but actually contains folded layers of radioactive material inside.  It can produce electricity for several years at a steady voltage… but it's barely enough to power a small LED, and these batteries were worth hundreds of dollars.  Mostly they're a good way to brag to your neighbours that you have a nuclear power source in your house."

msgid "Did your neighbors brag about their cool beta-decay-powered nightlights?  Do them one better!  The CuppaTech 4 radioisotope thermoelectric generator is a three kilogram chunk of metal - mostly lead - with a slug of cerium-244 encased within.  It is capable of generating somewhere between 100-150 Watts of thermal energy, although its electrical generation capacity is minimal at only 2 Watts.  Careful!  Curium is great at making heat, and also releases deadly gamma radiation.  Keep away from cellular life forms."
msgstr "Did your neighbours brag about their cool beta-decay-powered nightlights?  Do them one better!  The CuppaTech 4 radioisotope thermoelectric generator is a three kilogram chunk of metal - mostly lead - with a slug of cerium-244 encased within.  It is capable of generating somewhere between 100-150 Watts of thermal energy, although its electrical generation capacity is minimal at only 2 Watts.  Careful!  Curium is great at making heat, and also releases deadly gamma radiation.  Keep away from cellular life forms."

msgid "aluminum foil"
msgid_plural "aluminum foil"
msgstr[0] "aluminium foil"
msgstr[1] "aluminium foil"

msgid "A sheet of thin foil made of aluminum.  Sometimes called 'tin foil' due to being made of tin in the past."
msgstr "A sheet of thin foil made of aluminium.  Sometimes called 'tin foil' due to being made of tin in the past."

msgid "plant fiber"
msgid_plural "plant fiber"
msgstr[0] "plant fibre"
msgstr[1] "plant fibre"

msgid "Tough, thin fiber taken from a plant.  Can be used as thread."
msgstr "Tough, thin fibre taken from a plant.  Can be used as thread."

