msgid "A hardcover English translation of the Kitáb-i-Íqán, also known as the Book of Certitude.  It was written by Baha'u'llah, the founder of the Baha'i Faith, and addresses theological and philosophical aspects of religion, provides guidance on understanding spiritual truth and recognizing divine messengers throughout history.  This book also explores themes such as the nature of God, the purpose of religion, the progression of revelation, and the spiritual significance of the Baha'i Faith in relation to other religions."
msgstr "A hardcover English translation of the Kitáb-i-Íqán, also known as the Book of Certitude.  It was written by Baha'u'llah, the founder of the Baha'i Faith, and addresses theological and philosophical aspects of religion, provides guidance on understanding spiritual truth and recognising divine messengers throughout history.  This book also explores themes such as the nature of God, the purpose of religion, the progression of revelation, and the spiritual significance of the Baha'i Faith in relation to other religions."

