msgid "The Sapra '36 is a short smoothbore bolt-action grenade launcher, fitted with a 5-round box magazine and a large, efficient muzzle brake.  Designed in the interwar period following the proliferation of Brogyeki '23, the Sapra was intended to assist in riots, ambushes and assaulting in urban operations, where explosives applied in quick succession could make short work of targets.  To further assist in riot operations, the Sapra can be fitted with a bayonet, a frivolity that the Exodii almost immediately discarded.  Unlike the Brogyeki, the Sapra is incapable of chambering the longer 27.3 x 110 Diyua shells.  The Exodii have replaced the stock with an aluminum alloy chassis, leaving behind the original wood ones as they became damaged."
msgstr "The Sapra '36 is a short smoothbore bolt-action grenade launcher, fitted with a 5-round box magazine and a large, efficient muzzle brake.  Designed in the interwar period following the proliferation of Brogyeki '23, the Sapra was intended to assist in riots, ambushes and assaulting in urban operations, where explosives applied in quick succession could make short work of targets.  To further assist in riot operations, the Sapra can be fitted with a bayonet, a frivolity that the Exodii almost immediately discarded.  Unlike the Brogyeki, the Sapra is incapable of chambering the longer 27.3 x 110 Diyua shells.  The Exodii have replaced the stock with an aluminium alloy chassis, leaving behind the original wood ones as they became damaged."

msgid "The Sapra '36 is a short smoothbore bolt-action grenade launcher, fitted with a 5-round box magazine and a large, efficient muzzle brake.  Designed in the interwar period following the proliferation of Brogyeki '23, the Sapra was intended to assist in riots, ambushes and assaulting in urban operations, where explosives applied in quick succession could make short work of targets.  To further assist in riot operations, the Sapra can be fitted with a bayonet, a frivolity that the Exodii almost immediately discarded.  Unlike the Brogyeki, the Sapra is incapable of chambering the longer 27.3x110 Diyua shells.  The Exodii have replaced the stock with an aluminum alloy chassis, leaving behind the original wood ones as they became damaged."
msgstr "The Sapra '36 is a short smoothbore bolt-action grenade launcher, fitted with a 5-round box magazine and a large, efficient muzzle brake.  Designed in the interwar period following the proliferation of Brogyeki '23, the Sapra was intended to assist in riots, ambushes and assaulting in urban operations, where explosives applied in quick succession could make short work of targets.  To further assist in riot operations, the Sapra can be fitted with a bayonet, a frivolity that the Exodii almost immediately discarded.  Unlike the Brogyeki, the Sapra is incapable of chambering the longer 27.3x110 Diyua shells.  The Exodii have replaced the stock with an aluminium alloy chassis, leaving behind the original wood ones as they became damaged."

msgid "Nothing but ruins and ash-choked skies remained in the world where this exotic weapon was manufactured, and the Exodii, ever pragmatic, choose not to explore beyond what was necessary to perform a second, emergency escape.  A single discharge from the Caotel easily melts through conventional armor and flash-incinerates anything behind it, but its state of disrepair limits the number of shots it can fire in quick succession."
msgstr "Nothing but ruins and ash-choked skies remained in the world where this exotic weapon was manufactured, and the Exodii, ever pragmatic, choose not to explore beyond what was necessary to perform a second, emergency escape.  A single discharge from the Caotel easily melts through conventional armour and flash-incinerates anything behind it, but its state of disrepair limits the number of shots it can fire in quick succession."

msgid "A cacophony of symbols flash across the weapon's display, but it seems to stabilize nonetheless."
msgstr "A cacophony of symbols flash across the weapon's display, but it seems to stabilise nonetheless."

msgid "Originally designed for naval defense of a small island country, this gun served Exodii as long as they existed, being one of its reliable tools in later stages of world decay.  Cheap ammunition, a simple mechanism, and immense power output would make it a great weapon for any survivor who is able to carry nearly a hundred kilo of its weight and is in need to penetrate a small bunker.  Unless your body is compatible with Exodii Standard Combat Bodyframe, you can only use it with a heavy-duty tripod, and only while prone.  Due to the size of a top-mounted magazine, the user needs to use a scope mounted on the side of a gun."
msgstr "Originally designed for naval defence of a small island country, this gun served Exodii as long as they existed, being one of its reliable tools in later stages of world decay.  Cheap ammunition, a simple mechanism, and immense power output would make it a great weapon for any survivor who is able to carry nearly a hundred kilo of its weight and is in need to penetrate a small bunker.  Unless your body is compatible with Exodii Standard Combat Bodyframe, you can only use it with a heavy-duty tripod, and only while prone.  Due to the size of a top-mounted magazine, the user needs to use a scope mounted on the side of a gun."

msgid "A large flamethrower with substantial gas reserves.  The steel frame, with canvas accoutrements and aluminum cylinders, are all colored olive drab, like so many other pieces of equipment from the Vietnam War era."
msgstr "A large flamethrower with substantial gas reserves.  The steel frame, with canvas accoutrements and aluminium cylinders, are all coloured olive drab, like so many other pieces of equipment from the Vietnam War era."

msgid "A modernized flamethrower, using alloy components and composite pressure tanks.  Despite having been replaced by the M202 FLASH, due to the questionable effectiveness of the flamethrower in modern combat, it appears that someone, somewhere, needed a flamethrower for the modern age, as the date code on many of the components is within the past five years.  While this resembles the Vietnam War era M9-7, the wand ignition system has been improved with a piezoelectric one, in addition to the material improvements of the system overall."
msgstr "A modernised flamethrower, using alloy components and composite pressure tanks.  Despite having been replaced by the M202 FLASH, due to the questionable effectiveness of the flamethrower in modern combat, it appears that someone, somewhere, needed a flamethrower for the modern age, as the date code on many of the components is within the past five years.  While this resembles the Vietnam War era M9-7, the wand ignition system has been improved with a piezoelectric one, in addition to the material improvements of the system overall."

msgid "Also called a Pennsylvania rifle, this long-barreled rifled flintlock gun has significantly increased accuracy at the cost of taking even longer to reload."
msgstr "Also called a Pennsylvania rifle, this long-barrelled rifled flintlock gun has significantly increased accuracy at the cost of taking even longer to reload."

msgid "The Hub 01 Hybrid Weapons Platform, or just the HWP.  With its combination of black-finished steel, blue polymer furniture, and a number of proprietary bolts and fasteners to hold the pieces in place, this weapon looks like it belongs in a science fiction movie.  The body has \"MULTI CALIBER\" inlaid in the steel, near a quick release used both to exchange the installed barrel and to change the magazine well's adapter."
msgstr "The Hub 01 Hybrid Weapons Platform, or just the HWP.  With its combination of black-finished steel, blue polymer furniture, and a number of proprietary bolts and fasteners to hold the pieces in place, this weapon looks like it belongs in a science fiction movie.  The body has \"MULTI CALIBRE\" inlaid in the steel, near a quick release used both to exchange the installed barrel and to change the magazine well's adaptor."

msgid "A weapons platform you don't recognize.  With its combination of black-finished steel, brown polymer furniture, and a number of proprietary bolts and fasteners to hold the pieces in place, this weapon looks like it belongs in a science fiction movie.  The body has \"XE\" inlaid in the steel."
msgstr "A weapons platform you don't recognise.  With its combination of black-finished steel, brown polymer furniture, and a number of proprietary bolts and fasteners to hold the pieces in place, this weapon looks like it belongs in a science fiction movie.  The body has \"XE\" inlaid in the steel."

msgid "HWP personal defense configuration"
msgid_plural "HWP personal defense configuration"
msgstr[0] "HWP personal defence configuration"
msgstr[1] "HWP personal defence configuration"

msgid "The Hub 01 Fire Support Platform, or just the FSP.  Like the Hybrid Weapons Platform, it combines black-finished aluminum, blue polymer furniture, and a number of proprietary bolts and fasteners for a sci-fi aesthetic.  The barrel is stamped with \"40x46mm LV\", and the magwell looks like it accepts some truly MASSIVE magazines, which the gun appears to be capable of emptying in semi-automatic or fully-automatic fashion."
msgstr "The Hub 01 Fire Support Platform, or just the FSP.  Like the Hybrid Weapons Platform, it combines black-finished aluminium, blue polymer furniture, and a number of proprietary bolts and fasteners for a sci-fi aesthetic.  The barrel is stamped with \"40x46mm LV\", and the magwell looks like it accepts some truly MASSIVE magazines, which the gun appears to be capable of emptying in semi-automatic or fully-automatic fashion."

msgid "A classic Mossberg 590 pump-action shotgun, modified by the manufacturer to utilize box magazines."
msgstr "A classic Mossberg 590 pump-action shotgun, modified by the manufacturer to utilise box magazines."

msgid "A home-made double-barreled shotgun.  It is simply two pipes attached to a stock, with a pair of hammers to strike the two rounds it holds."
msgstr "A home-made double-barrelled shotgun.  It is simply two pipes attached to a stock, with a pair of hammers to strike the two rounds it holds."

msgid "With over 10 million made, the Remington 870 is one of the most popular shotguns on the market, and finds use with hunters and law enforcement agencies alike thanks to its high accuracy and muzzle velocity.  This one is a 28 inch barreled model for hunting fowl and game."
msgstr "With over 10 million made, the Remington 870 is one of the most popular shotguns on the market, and finds use with hunters and law enforcement agencies alike thanks to its high accuracy and muzzle velocity.  This one is a 28 inch barrelled model for hunting fowl and game."

msgid "A 4-round pump-action shotgun, ones like these have existed for many decades, and are still very popular due to their reliability and lethality, whether for hunting or home defense."
msgstr "A 4-round pump-action shotgun, ones like these have existed for many decades, and are still very popular due to their reliability and lethality, whether for hunting or home defence."

msgid "This semi-automatic shotgun features a self compensating gas system that will feed a wide array of shells while also reducing recoil.  Introduced in 1963, it is favored by law enforcement, hunters and competition shooters, and has been the best-selling autoloading shotgun in U.S. history.  This is the nickel finished, teflon coated competition model, with a full length magazine tube and 30 inch barrel."
msgstr "This semi-automatic shotgun features a self compensating gas system that will feed a wide array of shells while also reducing recoil.  Introduced in 1963, it is favoured by law enforcement, hunters and competition shooters, and has been the best-selling autoloading shotgun in U.S. history.  This is the nickel finished, teflon coated competition model, with a full length magazine tube and 30 inch barrel."

msgid "A brother of more typical hunting style shotguns, this particular model was most often seen utilized for self-defense or law-enforcement purposes.  Featuring a shortened 18.5 inch barrel and extended 7-round magazine tube, it's a very versatile and reliable weapon."
msgstr "A brother of more typical hunting style shotguns, this particular model was most often seen utilised for self-defence or law-enforcement purposes.  Featuring a shortened 18.5 inch barrel and extended 7-round magazine tube, it's a very versatile and reliable weapon."

msgid "With over 10 million made, the Remington 870 is one of the most popular shotguns on the market, and finds use with hunters and law enforcement agencies alike thanks to its high accuracy and muzzle velocity.  This one is an 18.5 inch barreled defensive model."
msgstr "With over 10 million made, the Remington 870 is one of the most popular shotguns on the market, and finds use with hunters and law enforcement agencies alike thanks to its high accuracy and muzzle velocity.  This one is an 18.5 inch barrelled defensive model."

msgid "double-barreled shotgun"
msgid_plural "double-barreled shotguns"
msgstr[0] "double-barrelled shotgun"
msgstr[1] "double-barrelled shotguns"

msgid "The classic double-barreled shotgun, with the barrels arranged side-by-side.  It consists of little more than 2 barrels, a striker to hit the shell, and a wooden stock"
msgstr "The classic double-barrelled shotgun, with the barrels arranged side-by-side.  It consists of little more than 2 barrels, a striker to hit the shell, and a wooden stock"

msgid "An antique double-barreled shotgun chambered in 12 gauge.  These were made by many different manufacturers, but these inexpensive firearms were all sold in the Sears and Roebuck catalog in the days of yore."
msgstr "An antique double-barrelled shotgun chambered in 12 gauge.  These were made by many different manufacturers, but these inexpensive firearms were all sold in the Sears and Roebuck catalogue in the days of yore."

msgid "An antique double-barreled shotgun chambered in 12 gauge.  Not to be confused with the board game company of the same name, Parker Bros. made shotguns from 1867 to 1942, before they were phased out of production by Remington, who had acquired the company the previous decade.  These shotguns were sold in many different \"grades\" at varying price points, with higher quality of engravings being included at higher cost.  This particular shotgun is a \"Trojan\", which was the cheapest grade Parker Bros. sold."
msgstr "An antique double-barrelled shotgun chambered in 12 gauge.  Not to be confused with the board game company of the same name, Parker Bros. made shotguns from 1867 to 1942, before they were phased out of production by Remington, who had acquired the company the previous decade.  These shotguns were sold in many different \"grades\" at varying price points, with higher quality of engravings being included at higher cost.  This particular shotgun is a \"Trojan\", which was the cheapest grade Parker Bros. sold."

msgid "A relatively modern double-barreled shotgun chambered in 12 gauge.  \"CZ\" stands for \"Česká zbrojovka\", or Czech armory.  CZ's weapons are either Czech imports or produced by their US based subsidiaries.  This specific model is the Bobwhite, with a wooden stock and black chrome barrels."
msgstr "A relatively modern double-barrelled shotgun chambered in 12 gauge.  \"CZ\" stands for \"Česká zbrojovka\", or Czech armoury.  CZ's weapons are either Czech imports or produced by their US based subsidiaries.  This specific model is the Bobwhite, with a wooden stock and black chrome barrels."

msgid "triple-barreled shotgun"
msgid_plural "triple-barreled shotguns"
msgstr[0] "triple-barrelled shotgun"
msgstr[1] "triple-barrelled shotguns"

msgid "A single barreled 12 gauge shotgun with an 18.5 inch barrel, produced by H&R.  While Harrington and Richardson has gone through many different acquisitions, name changes, and bankruptcies, it produces the same or similar weapons that it did in the early 20th century.  This particular model, the 58, was mass-produced between 1974-1981."
msgstr "A single barrelled 12 gauge shotgun with an 18.5 inch barrel, produced by H&R.  While Harrington and Richardson has gone through many different acquisitions, name changes, and bankruptcies, it produces the same or similar weapons that it did in the early 20th century.  This particular model, the 58, was mass-produced between 1974-1981."

msgid "double-barreled pump shotgun"
msgid_plural "double-barreled pump shotguns"
msgstr[0] "double-barrelled pump shotgun"
msgstr[1] "double-barrelled pump shotguns"

msgid "A bullpup, 12-gauge, pump-action, double-barreled mouthful of a shotgun.  Each barrel feeds from its own magazine, making the weapon actually two firearms in a single frame, and, while each barrel has its own associated trigger, the presence of a single pump to actuate both mechanisms means that it cannot be used precisely.  This, however, isn't to say that the weapon isn't fit for the service of shooting zombies at point blank ranges."
msgstr "A bullpup, 12-gauge, pump-action, double-barrelled mouthful of a shotgun.  Each barrel feeds from its own magazine, making the weapon actually two firearms in a single frame, and, while each barrel has its own associated trigger, the presence of a single pump to actuate both mechanisms means that it cannot be used precisely.  This, however, isn't to say that the weapon isn't fit for the service of shooting zombies at point blank ranges."

msgid "The Winchester 1897 was one of the first commercially-successful pump-action shotguns.  In its 'trench' configuration it has become a heavily-romanticized American icon of World War I.  With its barrel shroud, bayonet lug, and 17 inch bayonet, this shotgun is undeniably fearsome in appearance.  There aren't any more trenches to clear, so the next zombie-infested town will have to suffice."
msgstr "The Winchester 1897 was one of the first commercially-successful pump-action shotguns.  In its 'trench' configuration it has become a heavily-romanticised American icon of World War I.  With its barrel shroud, bayonet lug, and 17 inch bayonet, this shotgun is undeniably fearsome in appearance.  There aren't any more trenches to clear, so the next zombie-infested town will have to suffice."

msgid "Workhorse, companion, and Italian hole-puncher: the M2 forms the backbone of the Benelli's venerable line of Super 90 shotguns, utilizing the company's signature inertia-driven system to snap out 12-gauge shells with alacrity.  Though possessing a 3-round magazine tube, the shotgun's dimpled, synthetic furniture, cryogenically treated barrel, and robust action capable of withstanding magnum loads make it a hardy option, even for the post-Cataclysm survivor."
msgstr "Workhorse, companion, and Italian hole-puncher: the M2 forms the backbone of the Benelli's venerable line of Super 90 shotguns, utilising the company's signature inertia-driven system to snap out 12-gauge shells with alacrity.  Though possessing a 3-round magazine tube, the shotgun's dimpled, synthetic furniture, cryogenically treated barrel, and robust action capable of withstanding magnum loads make it a hardy option, even for the post-Cataclysm survivor."

msgid "Not related to the Soviet weapon designer, Tokarev, this Turkish shotgun uses an AR-12 shotgun platform to make the user comfortably hold it like a rifle and to utilize MKA 1919 magazines of different sizes."
msgstr "Not related to the Soviet weapon designer, Tokarev, this Turkish shotgun uses an AR-12 shotgun platform to make the user comfortably hold it like a rifle and to utilise MKA 1919 magazines of different sizes."

