msgid "fencing saber"
msgid_plural "fencing sabers"
msgstr[0] "fencing sabre"
msgstr[1] "fencing sabres"

msgid "A weapon used for fencing, the most noble of all sports.  Not designed for combat the saber at least bears an edge and so outperforms the foil, though still lacks the weight of the épée."
msgstr "A weapon used for fencing, the most noble of all sports.  Not designed for combat the sabre at least bears an edge and so outperforms the foil, though still lacks the weight of the épée."

msgid "sharpened saber"
msgid_plural "sharpened sabers"
msgstr[0] "sharpened sabre"
msgstr[1] "sharpened sabres"

msgid "What was once a mostly-harmless fencing saber has had its rounded tip snapped off and has been crudely sharpened to a point.  Though it still lacks a cutting edge, it is now considerably more lethal, yet still familiar to the practiced fencer."
msgstr "What was once a mostly-harmless fencing sabre has had its rounded tip snapped off and has been crudely sharpened to a point.  Though it still lacks a cutting edge, it is now considerably more lethal, yet still familiar to the practiced fencer."

msgid "electrified saber"
msgid_plural "electrified sabers"
msgstr[0] "electrified sabre"
msgstr[1] "electrified sabres"

msgid "The modifications made to this fencing saber may not be sporting, but they might give you an edge in this final competition.  Extra effort has been made to insulate the grip and a high voltage stun gun has been attached to the guard, wired to the tip along the saber's groove.  Thrusting the sharpened tip into a foe and activating the momentary switch will deliver a painful electric shock."
msgstr "The modifications made to this fencing sabre may not be sporting, but they might give you an edge in this final competition.  Extra effort has been made to insulate the grip and a high voltage stun gun has been attached to the guard, wired to the tip along the sabre's groove.  Thrusting the sharpened tip into a foe and activating the momentary switch will deliver a painful electric shock."

