msgid "A 12-inch by 24-inch sheet of faux fur sewn together from mismatched patches.  Suitable for making clothing if you lack proper material sheets, but the bright, clashing colors might end up making you look like a diseased Muppet."
msgstr "A 12-inch by 24-inch sheet of faux fur sewn together from mismatched patches.  Suitable for making clothing if you lack proper material sheets, but the bright, clashing colours might end up making you look like a diseased Muppet."

msgid "A sheet of synthetic fabric blended with stretchy Lycra fibers, suitable for making flexible, yet strong clothing."
msgstr "A sheet of synthetic fabric blended with stretchy Lycra fibres, suitable for making flexible, yet strong clothing."

msgid "A small, 16-layer thick ballistic Kevlar panel.  This kind of Kevlar is precision-made by machine and features an extremely tight weave which cannot be replicated by hand.  Due to this, any damage incurred to your ballistic armor will necessitate complete replacement with a new panel.  It is not as effective as loose-woven Kevlar at stopping stab wounds, but it has no equal against the threat posed by firearms."
msgstr "A small, 16-layer thick ballistic Kevlar panel.  This kind of Kevlar is precision-made by machine and features an extremely tight weave which cannot be replicated by hand.  Due to this, any damage incurred to your ballistic armour will necessitate complete replacement with a new panel.  It is not as effective as loose-woven Kevlar at stopping stab wounds, but it has no equal against the threat posed by firearms."

msgid "A compressed panel of Kevlar treated with epoxy or other adhesive.  It could be used to repair items made of rigid Kevlar, and makes a decent substitute for damaged carbon fiber and the like even if it isn't exactly the same."
msgstr "A compressed panel of Kevlar treated with epoxy or other adhesive.  It could be used to repair items made of rigid Kevlar, and makes a decent substitute for damaged carbon fibre and the like even if it isn't exactly the same."

msgid "A pile of shredded fabric, dry grass, hair or other cheap materials which could be used to stuff the fabric layers of a gambeson to create armor more cheaply and easily than properly layering and quilting the entire product."
msgstr "A pile of shredded fabric, dry grass, hair or other cheap materials which could be used to stuff the fabric layers of a gambeson to create armour more cheaply and easily than properly layering and quilting the entire product."

msgid "Very durable Kevlar thread that would be particularly useful for making ballistic armor, though it's fine to use in place of normal thread too, in most cases.  Making armor-grade Kevlar sheets from this would need a particularly tight weave, and so would require some specialized machinery."
msgstr "Very durable Kevlar thread that would be particularly useful for making ballistic armour, though it's fine to use in place of normal thread too, in most cases.  Making armour-grade Kevlar sheets from this would need a particularly tight weave, and so would require some specialised machinery."

msgid "A strip of broad, flat cotton, 42 inches in length, with a metal adjustment buckle threaded in the center.  Normally used as a shoulder strap for bags, its ends are usually sown about a corresponding container's D-rings."
msgstr "A strip of broad, flat cotton, 42 inches in length, with a metal adjustment buckle threaded in the centre.  Normally used as a shoulder strap for bags, its ends are usually sown about a corresponding container's D-rings."

msgid "A wooden post with a 4 by 4 square base.  Posts with a length similar to this are commonly used in mailboxes or as table legs."
msgstr "A wooden post with a 4 by 4 square base.  Posts with a length similar to this are commonly used in postboxes or as table legs."

msgid "jumper cable"
msgid_plural "jumper cables"
msgstr[0] "jump lead"
msgstr[1] "jump leads"

msgid "A 3-foot (or about 1 m) jumper cable: a short multi-stranded copper cable with power leads on either end, whose main purpose is to share power between vehicles, but can also link other electrical systems."
msgstr "A 3-foot (or about 1 m) jump lead: a short multi-stranded copper cable with power leads on either end, whose main purpose is to share power between vehicles, but can also link other electrical systems."

msgid "heavy-duty jumper cable"
msgid_plural "heavy-duty jumper cables"
msgstr[0] "heavy-duty jump lead"
msgstr[1] "heavy-duty jump leads"

msgid "A long, thick, heavy-duty jumper cable with power leads on either end.  It looks like you could use it to hook up two vehicles to each other, though you expect the power loss would be noticeable.  Can also link other electrical systems."
msgstr "A long, thick, heavy-duty jump lead with power leads on either end.  It looks like you could use it to hook up two vehicles to each other, though you expect the power loss would be noticeable.  Can also link other electrical systems."

msgid "This is the cable of the gods: 100 meters long, no power loss, light as a feather, and fits in a matchbook.  You're sure this wasn't supposed to exist, and the way it shimmers makes you uneasy."
msgstr "This is the cable of the gods: 100 metres long, no power loss, light as a feather, and fits in a matchbook.  You're sure this wasn't supposed to exist, and the way it shimmers makes you uneasy."

msgid "A kit containing all the specialized knives you need to debone, skin, and prepare cuts of meat from an animal."
msgstr "A kit containing all the specialised knives you need to debone, skin, and prepare cuts of meat from an animal."

msgid "A sealed jar holding sanitized yeast wort.  You may harvest the yeast inside when it's done culturing."
msgstr "A sealed jar holding sanitised yeast wort.  You may harvest the yeast inside when it's done culturing."

msgid "gasoline cooker"
msgid_plural "gasoline cookers"
msgstr[0] "petrol cooker"
msgstr[1] "petrol cookers"

msgid "A simple heater powered by gasoline.  It is designed for cooking food."
msgstr "A simple heater powered by petrol.  It is designed for cooking food."

msgid "A high end hotplate that utilizes magnetic induction coils to heat ferrous cookware directly.  It is far more efficient than a standard hotplate."
msgstr "A high end hotplate that utilises magnetic induction coils to heat ferrous cookware directly.  It is far more efficient than a standard hotplate."

msgid "An ultra-light alcohol-burning stove with a simmer ring, crafted by hand from a couple of aluminum soda cans.  It comes with a 500 mL plastic bottle to hold concentrated alcohol fuel."
msgstr "An ultra-light alcohol-burning stove with a simmer ring, crafted by hand from a couple of aluminium soda cans.  It comes with a 500 mL plastic bottle to hold concentrated alcohol fuel."

msgid "A large pot with 20 gauge walls and a thick aluminum bottom, modified to serve as a bulky but passable pressure cooker."
msgstr "A large pot with 20 gauge walls and a thick aluminium bottom, modified to serve as a bulky but passable pressure cooker."

msgid "crystallizing sugar"
msgid_plural "crystallizing sugars"
msgstr[0] "crystallising sugar"
msgstr[1] "crystallising sugars"

msgid "Sweet, sweet sugar in the process of crystallizing.  It needs two weeks to form solid crystals."
msgstr "Sweet, sweet sugar in the process of crystallising.  It needs two weeks to form solid crystals."

msgid "You break up the crystallized sugar into a coarse powder."
msgstr "You break up the crystallised sugar into a coarse powder."

msgid "The sugar is still crystallizing."
msgstr "The sugar is still crystallising."

msgid "A floor-mounted machine containing all the levers, clamps, and mounts required to remove or fit a tire, plus an integrated foot pump to inflate it."
msgstr "A floor-mounted machine containing all the levers, clamps, and mounts required to remove or fit a tyre, plus an integrated foot pump to inflate it."

msgid "A 35 mm digital SLR (single-lens reflex) camera with optical and digital viewfinders, a zoom lens with auto-focus and stabilizer, and flash.  You can look at your photos on the digital screen or transfer them with any standard electronic device.  Before the Cataclysm, you could have taken professional-grade photos using this."
msgstr "A 35 mm digital SLR (single-lens reflex) camera with optical and digital viewfinders, a zoom lens with auto-focus and stabiliser, and flash.  You can look at your photos on the digital screen or transfer them with any standard electronic device.  Before the Cataclysm, you could have taken professional-grade photos using this."

msgid "A tablet PC using an efficient color e-ink display.  Before the Cataclysm, these were nifty gadgets; now, they are extremely useful tools.  Runs on conventional batteries."
msgstr "A tablet PC using an efficient colour e-ink display.  Before the Cataclysm, these were nifty gadgets; now, they are extremely useful tools.  Runs on conventional batteries."

msgid "This strange contraption appears to be little more than a laminated box built around a battery, a poorly backlit screen, and a wound spool of cloth netting.  The letters \"X E D R A\" are emblazoned on the side.  To operate the device, unfurl the netting and place it around the object to analyze.  Despite not appearing to do anything, it consumes an enormous amount of electricity and provides a brief numerical readout."
msgstr "This strange contraption appears to be little more than a laminated box built around a battery, a poorly backlit screen, and a wound spool of cloth netting.  The letters \"X E D R A\" are emblazoned on the side.  To operate the device, unfurl the netting and place it around the object to analyse.  Despite not appearing to do anything, it consumes an enormous amount of electricity and provides a brief numerical readout."

msgid "A unified power supply, or UPS.  It is a device developed jointly by military and scientific interests for use in combat and the field.  The UPS is designed to power tools, smartphones, armor, and some guns, but drains batteries quickly."
msgstr "A unified power supply, or UPS.  It is a device developed jointly by military and scientific interests for use in combat and the field.  The UPS is designed to power tools, smartphones, armour, and some guns, but drains batteries quickly."

msgid "A unified power supply, or UPS.  It is a device developed jointly by military and scientific interests for use in combat and the field.  The UPS is designed to power tools, smartphones, armor, and some guns, but drains batteries quickly.  Use it to turn it on."
msgstr "A unified power supply, or UPS.  It is a device developed jointly by military and scientific interests for use in combat and the field.  The UPS is designed to power tools, smartphones, armour, and some guns, but drains batteries quickly.  Use it to turn it on."

msgid "A direct methanol fuel cell which can provide power to UPS-compatible electronic devices by oxidizing methanol supplied from a specialized fuel tank to produce electricity."
msgstr "A direct methanol fuel cell which can provide power to UPS-compatible electronic devices by oxidising methanol supplied from a specialised fuel tank to produce electricity."

msgid "The M72 LAW (Light Anti-armor Weapon) is a one-time use lightweight rocket launcher, meant to take out tanks and other armored vehicles.  Designed to replace the earlier Bazookas, it features a shaped-charge warhead to pierce armor.  Though weaker than the more modern and heavier AT4, it's still in service to this day.  Due to its design, you must unpack it to use it, and it cannot be reloaded.  Activate to unpack."
msgstr "The M72 LAW (Light Anti-armour Weapon) is a one-time use lightweight rocket launcher, meant to take out tanks and other armoured vehicles.  Designed to replace the earlier Bazookas, it features a shaped-charge warhead to pierce armour.  Though weaker than the more modern and heavier AT4, it's still in service to this day.  Due to its design, you must unpack it to use it, and it cannot be reloaded.  Activate to unpack."

msgid "A specialized grenade designed to scramble robots' IFF control chips.  This converts the robot to your side for a short time, before the backup systems kick in.  Use this item to pull the pin and start the fuse, turning it into an active scrambler grenade."
msgstr "A specialised grenade designed to scramble robots' IFF control chips.  This converts the robot to your side for a short time, before the backup systems kick in.  Use this item to pull the pin and start the fuse, turning it into an active scrambler grenade."

msgid "A pear-shaped chunk of rocket candy obtained by heating saltpeter with sugar and casting the obtained liquid.  Can serve as a rocket fuel, but also as a smokescreen - if you light the narrow end, you should be able to throw it before the flame reaches the broad end."
msgstr "A pear-shaped chunk of rocket candy obtained by heating saltpetre with sugar and casting the obtained liquid.  Can serve as a rocket fuel, but also as a smokescreen - if you light the narrow end, you should be able to throw it before the flame reaches the broad end."

msgid "A small container for holding tinder, with holes punched in it to provide a controlled airflow.  It can nurture a smoldering ember for a long time, to start fires without modern tools."
msgstr "A small container for holding tinder, with holes punched in it to provide a controlled airflow.  It can nurture a smouldering ember for a long time, to start fires without modern tools."

msgid "A small container for holding tinder, with holes punched in it to provide a controlled airflow.  An ember is smoldering inside it, and can be used to start a campfire."
msgstr "A small container for holding tinder, with holes punched in it to provide a controlled airflow.  An ember is smouldering inside it, and can be used to start a campfire."

msgid "A short, lightweight emergency tool with a quarter-circular blade, a short pick opposite the blade, and an insulated handle.  Used on airplanes to chop down or pry walls or cabinets to gain access in case of a fire."
msgstr "A short, lightweight emergency tool with a quarter-circular blade, a short pick opposite the blade, and an insulated handle.  Used on aeroplanes to chop down or pry walls or cabinets to gain access in case of a fire."

msgid "A handheld fire extinguisher containing a liter of highly compressed CO2 gas.  Useful for putting out adjacent fires."
msgstr "A handheld fire extinguisher containing a litre of highly compressed CO2 gas.  Useful for putting out adjacent fires."

msgid "A durable tool consisting of a sturdy fiberglass shaft tipped with a small steel hook."
msgstr "A durable tool consisting of a sturdy fibreglass shaft tipped with a small steel hook."

msgid "A durable tool consisting of a sturdy fiberglass shaft tipped with a set of 3 hooks, one large opposed by two small.  Hot sticks are used to maintain some standoff distance when manual manipulation of explosives is necessary, and robot assistance is unavailable."
msgstr "A durable tool consisting of a sturdy fibreglass shaft tipped with a set of 3 hooks, one large opposed by two small.  Hot sticks are used to maintain some standoff distance when manual manipulation of explosives is necessary, and robot assistance is unavailable."

msgid "A collection of items improvised for field reloading of shotshells.  A plank with a hole cut in the center, a medium-sized nail, and a whittled dowel are used to seat wads, decap primers, and (carefully!) reprime hulls.  Powder and shot are measured with a cut-down shotshell hull.  The opposite side of the plank has been shaped to allow for roll-crimping of the plastic hulls.  There's no provision for resizing, so reloaded hulls will fire best in the firearm they were fired from."
msgstr "A collection of items improvised for field reloading of shotshells.  A plank with a hole cut in the centre, a medium-sized nail, and a whittled dowel are used to seat wads, decap primers, and (carefully!) reprime hulls.  Powder and shot are measured with a cut-down shotshell hull.  The opposite side of the plank has been shaped to allow for roll-crimping of the plastic hulls.  There's no provision for resizing, so reloaded hulls will fire best in the firearm they were fired from."

msgid "internal gasoline tank"
msgid_plural "internal gasoline tanks"
msgstr[0] "internal petrol tank"
msgstr[1] "internal petrol tanks"

msgid "The internal tank for a gasoline fuel cell bionic."
msgstr "The internal tank for a petrol fuel cell bionic."

msgid "A cordless, double-sided, gasoline-powered hedge trimmer.  A long line of sharp-edged teeth extends from the engine; turning the trimmer on will make them rapidly vibrate.  The poor man's chainsaw as far as the zombies are concerned."
msgstr "A cordless, double-sided, petrol-powered hedge trimmer.  A long line of sharp-edged teeth extends from the engine; turning the trimmer on will make them rapidly vibrate.  The poor man's chainsaw as far as the zombies are concerned."

msgid "A cordless, double-sided, gasoline-powered hedge trimmer.  It is currently on, ready to do some zombie topiary; use this item to turn it off."
msgstr "A cordless, double-sided, petrol-powered hedge trimmer.  It is currently on, ready to do some zombie topiary; use this item to turn it off."

msgid "A small waterproof flashlight with an aluminum handle, powered by batteries.  Can be attached to some diving masks and hoods."
msgstr "A small waterproof flashlight with an aluminium handle, powered by batteries.  Can be attached to some diving masks and hoods."

msgid "A small waterproof high-power flashlight with an aluminum handle, powered by batteries.  Can be attached to some diving masks and hoods."
msgstr "A small waterproof high-power flashlight with an aluminium handle, powered by batteries.  Can be attached to some diving masks and hoods."

msgid "gasoline lantern (off)"
msgid_plural "gasoline lanterns (off)"
msgstr[0] "petrol lantern (off)"
msgstr[1] "petrol lanterns (off)"

msgid "A small gasoline-powered lantern.  It does not provide much light, but it lasts a long time.  Use it to turn it on."
msgstr "A small petrol-powered lantern.  It does not provide much light, but it lasts a long time.  Use it to turn it on."

msgid "gasoline lantern (on)"
msgid_plural "gasoline lanterns (on)"
msgstr[0] "petrol lantern (on)"
msgstr[1] "petrol lanterns (on)"

msgid "A small gasoline-powered lantern.  It does not provide much light, but it lasts a long time.  It is turned on.  Use it to turn it off."
msgstr "A small petrol-powered lantern.  It does not provide much light, but it lasts a long time.  It is turned on.  Use it to turn it off."

msgid "25 feet of colorful LED strip, that are often used as house lights or on some holidays."
msgstr "25 feet of colourful LED strip, that are often used as house lights or on some holidays."

msgid "A kerosene-fueled lamp.  It does not provide much light, but it lasts a long time.  Use it to turn it on."
msgstr "A kerosene-fuelled lamp.  It does not provide much light, but it lasts a long time.  Use it to turn it on."

msgid "A kerosene-fueled lamp.  It does not provide much light, but it lasts a long time.  It is turned on.  Use it to turn it off."
msgstr "A kerosene-fuelled lamp.  It does not provide much light, but it lasts a long time.  It is turned on.  Use it to turn it off."

msgid "A specialized small clay container with a wick, an ancient form of oil lamp.  Unlike newer designs, it isn't windproof, so the flame is likely to be extinguished if exposed to wind; better use it indoors.  It does not provide much light, but it lasts a long time.  Use it to light it."
msgstr "A specialised small clay container with a wick, an ancient form of oil lamp.  Unlike newer designs, it isn't windproof, so the flame is likely to be extinguished if exposed to wind; better use it indoors.  It does not provide much light, but it lasts a long time.  Use it to light it."

msgid "A specialized small clay container with a wick, an ancient form of oil lamp.  Unlike newer designs, it isn't windproof, so the flame is likely to be extinguished if exposed to wind; better use it indoors.  It does not provide much light, but lasts a long time.  It is lit, consuming oil and providing light.  Use it to extinguish the flame."
msgstr "A specialised small clay container with a wick, an ancient form of oil lamp.  Unlike newer designs, it isn't windproof, so the flame is likely to be extinguished if exposed to wind; better use it indoors.  It does not provide much light, but lasts a long time.  It is lit, consuming oil and providing light.  Use it to extinguish the flame."

msgid "An antique brass lamp designed to run from a pressurized cylinder of acetylene.  It is an efficient, if somewhat dangerous, light source."
msgstr "An antique brass lamp designed to run from a pressurised cylinder of acetylene.  It is an efficient, if somewhat dangerous, light source."

msgid "A construction tool for cutting through concrete or other surfaces.  It runs on gasoline.  Using this item will cause it to turn on, turning it into a very powerful but unwieldy melee weapon or a terrible chainsaw."
msgstr "A construction tool for cutting through concrete or other surfaces.  It runs on petrol.  Using this item will cause it to turn on, turning it into a very powerful but unwieldy melee weapon or a terrible chainsaw."

msgid "anesthesia kit"
msgid_plural "anesthesia kits"
msgstr[0] "anaesthesia kit"
msgstr[1] "anaesthesia kits"

msgid "A kit for inducing anesthesia for surgery, containing specialized canisters with a variety of powerful hypnotic, analgesic, and stimulative drugs.  It's intended for use in specialized medical equipment, and can't be administered manually."
msgstr "A kit for inducing anaesthesia for surgery, containing specialised canisters with a variety of powerful hypnotic, analgesic, and stimulative drugs.  It's intended for use in specialised medical equipment, and can't be administered manually."

msgid "A piece of cloth treated with a bleach solution to sterilize it for use as a bandage."
msgstr "A piece of cloth treated with a bleach solution to sterilise it for use as a bandage."

msgid "A piece of cloth boiled in water to sterilize it for use as a bandage."
msgstr "A piece of cloth boiled in water to sterilise it for use as a bandage."

msgid "A decent-sized piece of cotton, sterilized and sealed.  It's designed for medical purposes."
msgstr "A decent-sized piece of cotton, sterilised and sealed.  It's designed for medical purposes."

msgid "Liquid bandage for minor cuts and scrapes, packaged in a tiny bottle with an atomizer spray for convenient application."
msgstr "Liquid bandage for minor cuts and scrapes, packaged in a tiny bottle with an atomiser spray for convenient application."

msgid "A large, sealed plastic bag for liquids used in intravenous therapy, with rubber tube and cannula - all you need to perform an infusion.  Holds a liter of completely sterile saline, therefore it is safe to put it inside your veins, if you know how."
msgstr "A large, sealed plastic bag for liquids used in intravenous therapy, with rubber tube and cannula - all you need to perform an infusion.  Holds a litre of completely sterile saline, therefore it is safe to put it inside your veins, if you know how."

msgid "A huge, sealed plastic bag for liquids used in intravenous therapy, with rubber tube and cannula - all you need to perform an infusion.  Holds two liters of completely sterile saline, therefore it is safe to put it inside your veins, if you know how."
msgstr "A huge, sealed plastic bag for liquids used in intravenous therapy, with rubber tube and cannula - all you need to perform an infusion.  Holds two litres of completely sterile saline, therefore it is safe to put it inside your veins, if you know how."

msgid "A sheet of riveted chainmail.  With some skill, several of these sheets could be connected to make effective armor."
msgstr "A sheet of riveted chainmail.  With some skill, several of these sheets could be connected to make effective armour."

msgid "small sandcasting mold"
msgid_plural "small sandcasting molds"
msgstr[0] "small sandcasting mould"
msgstr[1] "small sandcasting moulds"

msgid "A small mold for casting molten metals into different shapes."
msgstr "A small mould for casting molten metals into different shapes."

msgid "large sandcasting mold"
msgid_plural "large sandcasting molds"
msgstr[0] "large sandcasting mould"
msgstr[1] "large sandcasting moulds"

msgid "A large mold for casting molten metals into different shapes."
msgstr "A large mould for casting molten metals into different shapes."

msgid "long sandcasting mold"
msgid_plural "long sandcasting molds"
msgstr[0] "long sandcasting mould"
msgstr[1] "long sandcasting moulds"

msgid "A large, long, mold for casting molten metals into different shapes."
msgstr "A large, long, mould for casting molten metals into different shapes."

msgid "sandcasting mold"
msgid_plural "sandcasting molds"
msgstr[0] "sandcasting mould"
msgstr[1] "sandcasting moulds"

msgid "A medium mold for casting molten metals into different shapes."
msgstr "A medium mould for casting molten metals into different shapes."

msgid "A gas-fueled metalworking forge.  With the right tools, you could use this for metalworking."
msgstr "A gas-fuelled metalworking forge.  With the right tools, you could use this for metalworking."

msgid "A non-refillable can of butane with an adapter for refilling lighters.  It could be useful as a fuel, but also as a solvent or chemical reagent."
msgstr "A non-refillable can of butane with an adaptor for refilling lighters.  It could be useful as a fuel, but also as a solvent or chemical reagent."

msgid "A stout, collapsible spade.  It's commonly used by military forces and favored by hikers for digging."
msgstr "A stout, collapsible spade.  It's commonly used by military forces and favoured by hikers for digging."

msgid "A pocket sized plastic canister filled with a pressurized tear gas spray, a step above oleoresin capsicum pepper spray in terms of potency.  Most commonly used by law enforcement and bear-wary hikers, but it became more common in recent months due to anxiety over the riots.  Probably won't do much against a zombie, but should give anything still breathing a rather nasty surprise and give you time to get away.  It contains enough spray for about twenty seconds of continuous application."
msgstr "A pocket sized plastic canister filled with a pressurised tear gas spray, a step above oleoresin capsicum pepper spray in terms of potency.  Most commonly used by law enforcement and bear-wary hikers, but it became more common in recent months due to anxiety over the riots.  Probably won't do much against a zombie, but should give anything still breathing a rather nasty surprise and give you time to get away.  It contains enough spray for about twenty seconds of continuous application."

msgid "A ten-foot aluminum stepladder.  Activate it to set it down."
msgstr "A ten-foot aluminium stepladder.  Activate it to set it down."

msgid "A remote control for an RC car, with a joystick to steer the car and colorful buttons that don't seem to do anything.  Perhaps they were for the deluxe model?"
msgstr "A remote control for an RC car, with a joystick to steer the car and colourful buttons that don't seem to do anything.  Perhaps they were for the deluxe model?"

msgid "A large machine used for extracting essential oils from large batches of organic material, producing a low-quality crude oil.  It consists of three long metal tubes funneled into a large drum that's set horizontally.  A series of hoses and tubes come out of the machine going to different valves.  It needs to be powered up to operate."
msgstr "A large machine used for extracting essential oils from large batches of organic material, producing a low-quality crude oil.  It consists of three long metal tubes funnelled into a large drum that's set horizontally.  A series of hoses and tubes come out of the machine going to different valves.  It needs to be powered up to operate."

msgid "A large makeshift appliance which captures nitrogen from the air for use in chemistry projects.  It includes a standard air filter for filtering out dust and other large particles, a deliquescent dryer to remove water vapor from air, and a nitrogen membrane filter to separate nitrogen from dry air."
msgstr "A large makeshift appliance which captures nitrogen from the air for use in chemistry projects.  It includes a standard air filter for filtering out dust and other large particles, a deliquescent dryer to remove water vapour from air, and a nitrogen membrane filter to separate nitrogen from dry air."

msgid "pressurized tank"
msgid_plural "pressurized tanks"
msgstr[0] "pressurised tank"
msgstr[1] "pressurised tanks"

msgid "A large steel cylinder used for storing pressurized gas.  It is marked with a faded, but legible O2 symbol."
msgstr "A large steel cylinder used for storing pressurised gas.  It is marked with a faded, but legible O2 symbol."

msgid "A hot plate with a metal housing attached.  The metal housing has a magnification viewport and a slot into which a capillary tube containing a crystallized sample is inserted.  The device lets you precisely measure the melting point of a crystal, a property very useful in identifying what it is and how pure it is."
msgstr "A hot plate with a metal housing attached.  The metal housing has a magnification viewport and a slot into which a capillary tube containing a crystallised sample is inserted.  The device lets you precisely measure the melting point of a crystal, a property very useful in identifying what it is and how pure it is."

msgid "Just looking at this thing makes you feel like a proper mad scientist.  It's a series of glass tubes and round flasks, connected to a central motor and a heating element.  The heating element warms one flask, kept rotating by the motor, evaporating the contents.  The vapor is then condensed in the tubes and collected in another flask, in case you wanted to save it for later."
msgstr "Just looking at this thing makes you feel like a proper mad scientist.  It's a series of glass tubes and round flasks, connected to a central motor and a heating element.  The heating element warms one flask, kept rotating by the motor, evaporating the contents.  The vapour is then condensed in the tubes and collected in another flask, in case you wanted to save it for later."

msgid "One of the classic pieces of mad science glassware, this is a small-volume still that passes vapor through a fractional distillation column and then condenses the distillate in a cooled collection column.  A grad student or a robot (is there really any difference?) collects the distillate in fractions so that specific contents can be analyzed.  Going a few milliliters at a time, it would not be very effective to try to distill whiskey in this thing."
msgstr "One of the classic pieces of mad science glassware, this is a small-volume still that passes vapour through a fractional distillation column and then condenses the distillate in a cooled collection column.  A grad student or a robot (is there really any difference?) collects the distillate in fractions so that specific contents can be analysed.  Going a few millilitres at a time, it would not be very effective to try to distil whiskey in this thing."

msgid "A small rectangular box.  Inside is a device that measures humidity by utilizing the hygroscopy of hair.  The hair's length changes with humidity as indicated on a dial."
msgstr "A small rectangular box.  Inside is a device that measures humidity by utilising the hygroscopy of hair.  The hair's length changes with humidity as indicated on a dial."

msgid "aluminum tent pole"
msgid_plural "aluminum tent poles"
msgstr[0] "aluminium tent pole"
msgstr[1] "aluminium tent poles"

msgid "A light, collapsible tent pole made from aluminum, perfect for pitching a tent."
msgstr "A light, collapsible tent pole made from aluminium, perfect for pitching a tent."

msgid "A mass-manufactured water pipe, otherwise known as a 'bong'.  It is colored with the 'rasta' pattern of red, yellow, and green."
msgstr "A mass-manufactured water pipe, otherwise known as a 'bong'.  It is coloured with the 'rasta' pattern of red, yellow, and green."

msgid "A device for spinning thread or yarn from fibers.  This particular model is electrically-powered and easily portable."
msgstr "A device for spinning thread or yarn from fibres.  This particular model is electrically-powered and easily portable."

msgid "A compact, lightweight shaving kit made for travelers.  You can use it to shave if it's supplied with soap.  It requires 1 unit of soap per use."
msgstr "A compact, lightweight shaving kit made for travellers.  You can use it to shave if it's supplied with soap.  It requires 1 unit of soap per use."

msgid "A simple loop snare, comprising a carefully wound loop of string, two anchor points, and a tool to hammer them in.  It is suitable for immobilizing only small animals.  It has no means of harming its target, as live meat lasts longer."
msgstr "A simple loop snare, comprising a carefully wound loop of string, two anchor points, and a tool to hammer them in.  It is suitable for immobilising only small animals.  It has no means of harming its target, as live meat lasts longer."

msgid "A bulky device that turns water and calcium carbide into unpressurized acetylene."
msgstr "A bulky device that turns water and calcium carbide into unpressurised acetylene."

