"  3.  In version 1 only you can dig trenches on all sides of the camp, which can possibly connect to the rooms on the sides to minimise the amount of trenching you need to do.\n"
"  4.  You can build various small features such as root cellars to preserve food or a radio tower to make it easier to recruit more companions.\n"
"  With each new construction in a modular camp can being able to be made from a different material you aren't constrained by what you start with.  If limited by resources, tents are a fast alternative way to provide shelter, but fragile and likely to get destroyed by the first zombie stumbling in, however the central building must still be made from a 'real' building material."

msgid ""
"You can build a faction camp in any kind of evac shelter.  Evac shelters are everywhere and often have fields surrounding them, so they're a little faster to start than a modular field camp but still make it easy to add expansions.\n"
"  Evac center camps can be built up in several ways.  You basically need to decide between building more bedrooms or adding crafting and cooking space."
msgstr ""
"You can build a faction camp in any kind of evac shelter.  Evac shelters are everywhere and often have fields surrounding them, so they're a little faster to start than a modular field camp but still make it easy to add expansions.\n"
"  Evac centre camps can be built up in several ways.  You basically need to decide between building more bedrooms or adding crafting and cooking space."

msgid ""
"A camp can have up to 8 expansions (one for each of the 8 adjacent overmap tiles).  Expansions add to the capabilities of your camp, such as adding a farm field or a manufactory for crafting all kinds of things.\n"
"  Expansion missions show up in separate tabs in the bulletin board, one set of missions per location, and you'll need to hit 'tab' to see them.  Some base camps have dedicated expansions tailored to their specific facilities, and while these might be accessible from other base camps should those be constructed adjacent to one of these, the set of reasonably general expansions are currently all limited to open field locations (field, hay field, farm field, or field dirt road).  The currently available general expansions are:\n"
"  -- Farm: This is a full tile of plowed fields that you can maintain or send companions on missions to maintain.  Plants grow here normally.  This expansion exists in two versions.\n"
"  -- Garage: This is a large building that currently doesn't provide any functionality, and so is of limited use (it used to provide disassembly before that was supported via zones, which can still be placed inside the garage).  This expansion exists in two versions.\n"
"  -- Canteen: This is an expanded kitchen, dining area, and pantry that provides an expanded set of companion cooking recipes.  This expansion exists in two versions.\n"
"  -- Livestock Area: This is a modular set of buildings for holding livestock such as cows, horses, or chickens.  Animals are not included!  This expansion exists in two versions.\n"
"  -- Fabrication Workshop: This is a large expansion for doing all kinds of crafts.  Companions can use some of the furniture in this expansion to craft some items much faster than you can do by yourself by hand.  This expansion exists in two versions.\n"
"  -- Central Storage Building: This is a large building for storing goods.  This expansion exists in two versions, the second of which allows the construction of storage furniture with a larger capacity than storage on the ground.\n"
"  Note that there is nothing stopping you from constructing more than one instance of an expansion, such as multiple farms for more farming, or a second Livestock expansion if you have a lot of animals.  In most cases there is not much value in having more than one of an expansion, though."
msgstr ""
"A camp can have up to 8 expansions (one for each of the 8 adjacent overmap tiles).  Expansions add to the capabilities of your camp, such as adding a farm field or a manufactory for crafting all kinds of things.\n"
"  Expansion missions show up in separate tabs in the bulletin board, one set of missions per location, and you'll need to hit 'tab' to see them.  Some base camps have dedicated expansions tailored to their specific facilities, and while these might be accessible from other base camps should those be constructed adjacent to one of these, the set of reasonably general expansions are currently all limited to open field locations (field, hay field, farm field, or field dirt road).  The currently available general expansions are:\n"
"  -- Farm: This is a full tile of ploughed fields that you can maintain or send companions on missions to maintain.  Plants grow here normally.  This expansion exists in two versions.\n"
"  -- Garage: This is a large building that currently doesn't provide any functionality, and so is of limited use (it used to provide disassembly before that was supported via zones, which can still be placed inside the garage).  This expansion exists in two versions.\n"
"  -- Canteen: This is an expanded kitchen, dining area, and pantry that provides an expanded set of companion cooking recipes.  This expansion exists in two versions.\n"
"  -- Livestock Area: This is a modular set of buildings for holding livestock such as cows, horses, or chickens.  Animals are not included!  This expansion exists in two versions.\n"
"  -- Fabrication Workshop: This is a large expansion for doing all kinds of crafts.  Companions can use some of the furniture in this expansion to craft some items much faster than you can do by yourself by hand.  This expansion exists in two versions.\n"
"  -- Central Storage Building: This is a large building for storing goods.  This expansion exists in two versions, the second of which allows the construction of storage furniture with a larger capacity than storage on the ground.\n"
"  Note that there is nothing stopping you from constructing more than one instance of an expansion, such as multiple farms for more farming, or a second Livestock expansion if you have a lot of animals.  In most cases there is not much value in having more than one of an expansion, though."

msgid ""
"Starting a camp doesn't take much time, and you can use a faction camp to keep your companions fed without needing to regularly give them food, so it's a good idea to establish a minimal camp anywhere you intend to be for a while.\n"
"  How much you want to expand your camps is up to you.  A modular field camp can be very resource intensive, but building one up allows you to send companions off to hunt and farm for you, so there's quite the pay-off.  What kind of camp (or camps) you want to build depends both on what you intend to focus on and whether you want to be stationary or roaming with stops in areas only for some time before moving on.  If nothing else, you should consider building a water well as soon as you can, which may require you to perform construction prerequisites.\n"
"  If you have access to a fire station or evac shelter, you may want to build your camp in them.  Both of those camps are very compact, but have much of the same functionality as an upgraded field camp without requiring so many resources.\n"
"  If you are adding expansions to your camp, consider starting with a farm, canteen, or fabrication workshop.  The farm makes it easy to grow your own food if you don't have any ready plowed farms nearby, the canteen provides you with a well and root cellars after some upgrades, while the fabrication workshop can allow you to craft some of the resources you need to upgrade your camp.\n"
"  The livestock area and the storage area probably shouldn't be your first expansions, but they both have their uses."
msgstr ""
"Starting a camp doesn't take much time, and you can use a faction camp to keep your companions fed without needing to regularly give them food, so it's a good idea to establish a minimal camp anywhere you intend to be for a while.\n"
"  How much you want to expand your camps is up to you.  A modular field camp can be very resource intensive, but building one up allows you to send companions off to hunt and farm for you, so there's quite the pay-off.  What kind of camp (or camps) you want to build depends both on what you intend to focus on and whether you want to be stationary or roaming with stops in areas only for some time before moving on.  If nothing else, you should consider building a water well as soon as you can, which may require you to perform construction prerequisites.\n"
"  If you have access to a fire station or evac shelter, you may want to build your camp in them.  Both of those camps are very compact, but have much of the same functionality as an upgraded field camp without requiring so many resources.\n"
"  If you are adding expansions to your camp, consider starting with a farm, canteen, or fabrication workshop.  The farm makes it easy to grow your own food if you don't have any ready ploughed farms nearby, the canteen provides you with a well and root cellars after some upgrades, while the fabrication workshop can allow you to craft some of the resources you need to upgrade your camp.\n"
"  The livestock area and the storage area probably shouldn't be your first expansions, but they both have their uses."

msgid "May you find your peace, traveler."
msgstr "May you find your peace, traveller."

msgid "Wow!  Such an honor to meet you in person!"
msgstr "Wow!  Such an honour to meet you in person!"

msgid "The great Foodperson in the flesh!  Such an honor to finally meet you in person!"
msgstr "The great Foodperson in the flesh!  Such an honour to finally meet you in person!"

msgid "This is no place for a civilian.  You should go to the refugee center."
msgstr "This is no place for a civilian.  You should go to the refugee centre."

msgid "A collection of mentally and physically disadvantaged survivors who beg for food in the Evac Center lobby."
msgstr "A collection of mentally and physically disadvantaged survivors who beg for food in the Evac Centre lobby."

msgid "Diverse bands, congregations and organizations with the common goal of preaching human survival through symbiosis with fungaloids."
msgstr "Diverse bands, congregations and organisations with the common goal of preaching human survival through symbiosis with fungaloids."

msgid "If you're getting chased by a horde of zombies, try ducking into the subways and traveling a block or two before coming back up."
msgstr "If you're getting chased by a horde of zombies, try ducking into the subways and travelling a block or two before coming back up."

msgid "If there's a pool of acid blocking your way, trying tossing a junk item into it.  Eating up items will help neutralize the acid faster."
msgstr "If there's a pool of acid blocking your way, trying tossing a junk item into it.  Eating up items will help neutralise the acid faster."

msgid "Zombie brutes and hulks have really tough hide, but skeletal juggernauts with their bone plates are the worst.  Don't bother shooting at them with lower-caliber guns, the bullet will bounce right off!"
msgstr "Zombie brutes and hulks have really tough hide, but skeletal juggernauts with their bone plates are the worst.  Don't bother shooting at them with lower-calibre guns, the bullet will bounce right off!"

msgid "I hid in a dumpster once or twice.  I may smell bad, but I'm not dead, as they say."
msgstr "I hid in a skip once or twice.  I may smell bad, but I'm not dead, as they say."

msgid "When it comes to footwear, you've got two basic choices as far as I see it; sneakers, for running extra fast, or boots for durability.  Depends on your style, I guess."
msgstr "When it comes to footwear, you've got two basic choices as far as I see it; trainers, for running extra fast, or boots for durability.  Depends on your style, I guess."

msgid "I know they look dumb, but wearing a fanny pack gives you that extra bit of storage without encumbering you."
msgstr "I know they look dumb, but wearing a bum bag gives you that extra bit of storage without encumbering you."

msgid "It's a good idea to carry around a couple of empty bottles.  You can fill them up with water, gasoline, or whatever!"
msgstr "It's a good idea to carry around a couple of empty bottles.  You can fill them up with water, petrol, or whatever!"

msgid "If you're going to be playing with Molotov cocktails around a gas station, just make sure you're a long way from those pumps."
msgstr "If you're going to be playing with Molotov cocktails around a petrol station, just make sure you're a long way from those pumps."

msgid "While there's not much to loot, gas stations are a good source for gasoline, to power tools or to make Molotov cocktails."
msgstr "While there's not much to loot, petrol stations are a good source for petrol, to power tools or to make Molotov cocktails."

msgid "It's not like in the movies; shooting a gas pump won't make it explode.  But it WILL make it leak all over the place, which is a definite fire hazard."
msgstr "It's not like in the movies; shooting a petrol pump won't make it explode.  But it WILL make it leak all over the place, which is a definite fire hazard."

msgid "Next time you visit a grocery store, load up on canned goods.  They never go bad!"
msgstr "Next time you visit a grocery store, load up on tinned goods.  They never go bad!"

msgid "Load up on canned goods if you ever find a grocery store.  Cans never go bad!"
msgstr "Load up on tinned goods if you ever find a grocery store.  Cans never go bad!"

msgid "I've spent many nights in the changing rooms at the back of clothing stores.  Walls on four sides, far from the store's entrance, a corridor for easy defense… it's perfect!"
msgstr "I've spent many nights in the changing rooms at the back of clothing stores.  Walls on four sides, far from the store's entrance, a corridor for easy defence… it's perfect!"

msgid "I have a dream of raiding a military bunker, but zombies and armor are a scary mix.  And the sheer thought of being sprayed with bullets by a turret is giving me the shivers."
msgstr "I have a dream of raiding a military bunker, but zombies and armour are a scary mix.  And the sheer thought of being sprayed with bullets by a turret is giving me the shivers."

msgid "I've thought about raiding an ant hill before, but I realized it wasn't worth the risk.  I doubt they have any loot beyond some scraps of food, you know?"
msgstr "I've thought about raiding an ant hill before, but I realised it wasn't worth the risk.  I doubt they have any loot beyond some scraps of food, you know?"

msgid "Autodocs are probably your best bet to install bionics - if you can find one!  However, I heard they won't work if you don't bring anesthetics to put you in a sleep."
msgstr "Autodocs are probably your best bet to install bionics - if you can find one!  However, I heard they won't work if you don't bring anaesthetics to put you in a sleep."

msgid "Civilization has made a step back in time, so let's learn from the past.  No fridges?  Build a root cellar or keep food cool in the basement.  No guns?  Make a pointy stick or a cudgel, and work from there.  The end of the world is not the end, it seems."
msgstr "Civilisation has made a step back in time, so let's learn from the past.  No fridges?  Build a root cellar or keep food cool in the basement.  No guns?  Make a pointy stick or a cudgel, and work from there.  The end of the world is not the end, it seems."

msgid "Heard a rumor that few cities were evacuated to a place that's not on the maps.  Tough luck finding them now.  But perhaps they don't want to be found.  Or worse - perhaps you don't know that you don't want to find them either, if you catch my drift."
msgstr "Heard a rumour that few cities were evacuated to a place that's not on the maps.  Tough luck finding them now.  But perhaps they don't want to be found.  Or worse - perhaps you don't know that you don't want to find them either, if you catch my drift."

msgid "Heard a rumor about a lady on rollerblades with a fire extinguisher strapped to her back.  Zipping around, hardly wearing no clothes, smashing cannibals in the face with a baseball bat.  Don't that beat all?"
msgstr "Heard a rumour about a lady on rollerblades with a fire extinguisher strapped to her back.  Zipping around, hardly wearing no clothes, smashing cannibals in the face with a baseball bat.  Don't that beat all?"

msgid "Ok, some weird shit now.  Before we met I saw a knight.  No, I'm fine under the hood.  A guy in a full medieval armor was cornered by some zombies.  Much to be said, but half an hour later, he was still alive.  Guess you can take a punch being a walking tin can."
msgstr "Ok, some weird shit now.  Before we met I saw a knight.  No, I'm fine under the hood.  A guy in a full medieval armour was cornered by some zombies.  Much to be said, but half an hour later, he was still alive.  Guess you can take a punch being a walking tin can."

msgid "There's no rule against wearing more than one set of pants.  Well, I mean, there probably is, but nothing stopping you from breaking it!"
msgstr "There's no rule against wearing more than one set of trousers.  Well, I mean, there probably is, but nothing stopping you from breaking it!"

msgid "Does our flag still yet wave?  We're battered but not yet out of the fight, we need the old colors!"
msgstr "Does our flag still yet wave?  We're battered but not yet out of the fight, we need the old colours!"

msgid "Analyze Zombie Blood"
msgstr "Analyse Zombie Blood"

msgid "I've heard some bad rumors so I hope you are up for another challenge…"
msgstr "I've heard some bad rumours so I hope you are up for another challenge…"

msgid "Apparently one of the other survivors picked up on an unusually dense horde of undead moving into the area.  At the center of this throng there was a 'leader' of some sort.  The short of it is, kill the son of a bitch.  We don't know what it is capable of or why it is surrounded by other zombies but this thing reeks of trouble.  Do whatever it takes but we can't risk it getting away."
msgstr "Apparently one of the other survivors picked up on an unusually dense horde of undead moving into the area.  At the centre of this throng there was a 'leader' of some sort.  The short of it is, kill the son of a bitch.  We don't know what it is capable of or why it is surrounded by other zombies but this thing reeks of trouble.  Do whatever it takes but we can't risk it getting away."

msgid "Traveling the backroads would be a good way to search for one."
msgstr "Travelling the backroads would be a good way to search for one."

msgid "Break into armory to retrieve family photo"
msgstr "Break into armoury to retrieve family photo"

msgid "I need you to get my family photo from the armory safe."
msgstr "I need you to get my family photo from the armoury safe."

msgid "I left the only photo I have from my family in the armory.  I don't have the code, can you get in?"
msgstr "I left the only photo I have from my family in the armoury.  I don't have the code, can you get in?"

msgid "Bring the pyromaniac to <color_light_blue>their rival's house</color> and don't forget to <color_yellow>bring at least 200 units of gasoline</color>.  After you got there, talk to the pyromaniac to start burning the house."
msgstr "Bring the pyromaniac to <color_light_blue>their rival's house</color> and don't forget to <color_yellow>bring at least 200 units of petrol</color>.  After you got there, talk to the pyromaniac to start burning the house."

msgid "Good.  Let's go to his house and goddamn burn it down!  Oh, by the way, could you bring gasoline with you, <name_g>?  I was so angry I forgot to bring it with me…"
msgstr "Good.  Let's go to his house and goddamn burn it down!  Oh, by the way, could you bring petrol with you, <name_g>?  I was so angry I forgot to bring it with me…"

msgid "Maybe we can find some gasoline at a gas station."
msgstr "Maybe we can find some petrol at a petrol station."

msgid "Center of the storm"
msgstr "Centre of the storm"

msgid "This is the center of the portal storm, you could find it upside down, dizzy and blindfolded.  Its presence is too altered to allow the mercy of ignorance."
msgstr "This is the centre of the portal storm, you could find it upside down, dizzy and blindfolded.  Its presence is too altered to allow the mercy of ignorance."

msgid "What, don't you remember?  No, sorry, that's not fair, it was a weird time.  OK, well, I guess this all started with the riots, didn't it?  We were just leading our lives, doing our jobs, and then people started rioting.  Not the usual protests that turned violent or anything, either, people just left their houses and started breaking shit.  The news tried to downplay it but they couldn't keep it off the internet.  I don't know what caused it, they said it was some kind of drug or toxin in the water?  Still, I didn't really realize how bad it was getting at first.  Somewhere along the way the \"rioters\" started getting up and walking around with holes in their chests, and that's when the real panic took over.  The next few days - or weeks, not really sure - are a blur to me.  You'd have to ask someone else how we got from there to total collapse."
msgstr "What, don't you remember?  No, sorry, that's not fair, it was a weird time.  OK, well, I guess this all started with the riots, didn't it?  We were just leading our lives, doing our jobs, and then people started rioting.  Not the usual protests that turned violent or anything, either, people just left their houses and started breaking shit.  The news tried to downplay it but they couldn't keep it off the internet.  I don't know what caused it, they said it was some kind of drug or toxin in the water?  Still, I didn't really realise how bad it was getting at first.  Somewhere along the way the \"rioters\" started getting up and walking around with holes in their chests, and that's when the real panic took over.  The next few days - or weeks, not really sure - are a blur to me.  You'd have to ask someone else how we got from there to total collapse."

msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid "A big-ass hole opened up right in the middle of town, and a nightmarish demon crawled out, right in front of the church.  We unloaded into it, but bullets just bounced off.  Got some civilians in the crossfire.  It started just devouring people like potato chips into a gullet that looked like a rotting asshole with teeth, and… well, I lost my nerve.  I ran.  I think I might have been the only person to escape.  I haven't been able to even look at my badge since then."
msgstr "A big-ass hole opened up right in the middle of town, and a nightmarish demon crawled out, right in front of the church.  We unloaded into it, but bullets just bounced off.  Got some civilians in the crossfire.  It started just devouring people like crisps into a gullet that looked like a rotting arsehole with teeth, and… well, I lost my nerve.  I ran.  I think I might have been the only person to escape.  I haven't been able to even look at my badge since then."

