msgid "Remnants of Civilization"
msgstr "Remnants of Civilisation"

msgid "A jewelry store should have a pair.  If not, I'd check a wedding venue."
msgstr "A jewellery store should have a pair.  If not, I'd check a wedding venue."

msgid "I've assembled quite a collection of evidence in my research, and I want an easier way to organize it.  If you could get me one of those e-ink tablets, I could scan all my documents into an easily-preserved digital format.  There's some money for you, too."
msgstr "I've assembled quite a collection of evidence in my research, and I want an easier way to organise it.  If you could get me one of those e-ink tablets, I could scan all my documents into an easily-preserved digital format.  There's some money for you, too."

msgid "Here's the money I promised you.  I'll start organizing my collection."
msgstr "Here's the money I promised you.  I'll start organising my collection."

msgid "Blasphemy, heresy, the righteous judgment of God!  I have found the scum of Hell pillaging a church for valuables!  Even in <the_cataclysm>, I shall not stand for this.  I want you to go there and wipe those <freaking> <name_b>s from the Earth."
msgstr "Blasphemy, heresy, the righteous judgement of God!  I have found the scum of Hell pillaging a church for valuables!  Even in <the_cataclysm>, I shall not stand for this.  I want you to go there and wipe those <freaking> <name_b>s from the Earth."

msgid "Righteous judgment shall come!"
msgstr "Righteous judgement shall come!"

msgid "Investigate the Center"
msgstr "Investigate the Centre"

msgid "I've had a bad run of things.  I grew up real poor, in a bad part of town, always got my nose where it shouldn't have been.  When I was about eighteen, I started doing coke heavily.  Every two days, I'd get spaced out on the stuff; started robbing gas stations and dumb <freaking> things like that for a fix.  I went to jail, and I met the New England Church Community there.  I joined up to find penance for my sins.  Another thing, stay off of that <freaking> stuff; I messed up my brain real bad doin' that."
msgstr "I've had a bad run of things.  I grew up real poor, in a bad part of town, always got my nose where it shouldn't have been.  When I was about eighteen, I started doing coke heavily.  Every two days, I'd get spaced out on the stuff; started robbing petrol stations and dumb <freaking> things like that for a fix.  I went to jail, and I met the New England Church Community there.  I joined up to find penance for my sins.  Another thing, stay off of that <freaking> stuff; I messed up my brain real bad doin' that."

msgid "Welcome, <granny_name_g>.  I don't think I recognize you, I'm Theresa."
msgstr "Welcome, <granny_name_g>.  I don't think I recognise you, I'm Theresa."

msgid "I was home alone during the ongoing riots.  My parents chose the worst possible time to reconnect, which sucks, but I'm also kinda happy for them.  Anyway, they were part of the NECC people, so they knew about this place and their plans and all.  Thing is, it was, like, really far away.  I kinda didn't want to go alone but I also didn't want the rioters to eat me, so I asked Sonia - my neighbor - to evacuate with me, I guess.  So that was fun; escaping my hometown, walking down the country road, waiting for a horror to ambush us.  Spoiler alert: we were attacked.  So this zombie shambles in front of us and Sonia whacks it real hard with her guitar!  Its brain splatters all over the pavement, I threw up 'cause it was so disgusting.  We got here soon after that.  My parents weren't here, obviously.  Oh man, they must worry about me so much…"
msgstr "I was home alone during the ongoing riots.  My parents chose the worst possible time to reconnect, which sucks, but I'm also kinda happy for them.  Anyway, they were part of the NECC people, so they knew about this place and their plans and all.  Thing is, it was, like, really far away.  I kinda didn't want to go alone but I also didn't want the rioters to eat me, so I asked Sonia - my neighbour - to evacuate with me, I guess.  So that was fun; escaping my hometown, walking down the country road, waiting for a horror to ambush us.  Spoiler alert: we were attacked.  So this zombie shambles in front of us and Sonia whacks it real hard with her guitar!  Its brain splatters all over the pavement, I threw up 'cause it was so disgusting.  We got here soon after that.  My parents weren't here, obviously.  Oh man, they must worry about me so much…"

msgid "Aren't you a bit too old not to realize how dangerous the world is for a kid like me?  I know how to handle one without hurting myself!  My dad taught me everything, he's a real pro."
msgstr "Aren't you a bit too old not to realise how dangerous the world is for a kid like me?  I know how to handle one without hurting myself!  My dad taught me everything, he's a real pro."

msgid "&Corrie blankly stares at the wall for a moment.  \"Me and my friends were in the cities when it hit, I was the only one to make it out.  Some gigantic horror… devoured… everything in its way.  There was a memorial service and all, organized by the church-goers.  By far the nicest thing they've done for me.\""
msgstr "&Corrie blankly stares at the wall for a moment.  \"Me and my friends were in the cities when it hit, I was the only one to make it out.  Some gigantic horror… devoured… everything in its way.  There was a memorial service and all, organised by the church-goers.  By far the nicest thing they've done for me.\""

msgid "It really isn't difficult to earn your money here.  Hard labor, like the rest of us."
msgstr "It really isn't difficult to earn your money here.  Hard labour, like the rest of us."

msgid "I've heard of unnatural monsters such as yourself causing chaos after the fall of civilization, and how men have transformed into horrors and gone mad with sin.  This is the judgment of God upon you heathens for your wicked ways, and I want nothing to do with it."
msgstr "I've heard of unnatural monsters such as yourself causing chaos after the fall of civilisation, and how men have transformed into horrors and gone mad with sin.  This is the judgement of God upon you heathens for your wicked ways, and I want nothing to do with it."

msgid "&Greenwood looks over his their shoulder, briefly glancing around before speaking in a low whisper.  \"Don't tell anyone I said this, but I don't like Helena at all.  Her father was a real nut, he'd rave on and on about an apocalypse he'd prepared for.  He always thought that his church would be the ark to weather the storm, that God would destroy the world by unleashing the armies of Hell; and he wasn't talking about the Second Coming of Christ.  Helena's just as fanatical as he was, and it reflects in her inadequate leadership.  To be honest, I'm highly concerned for some of the people here; they're obsessively zealous with Helena, and harbor a xenophobic hatred of everything.  As in Matthew 15:14, 'They are blind guides.  And if one blind person guides another, they will both fall into a pit'.\""
msgstr "&Greenwood looks over his their shoulder, briefly glancing around before speaking in a low whisper.  \"Don't tell anyone I said this, but I don't like Helena at all.  Her father was a real nut, he'd rave on and on about an apocalypse he'd prepared for.  He always thought that his church would be the ark to weather the storm, that God would destroy the world by unleashing the armies of Hell; and he wasn't talking about the Second Coming of Christ.  Helena's just as fanatical as he was, and it reflects in her inadequate leadership.  To be honest, I'm highly concerned for some of the people here; they're obsessively zealous with Helena, and harbour a xenophobic hatred of everything.  As in Matthew 15:14, 'They are blind guides.  And if one blind person guides another, they will both fall into a pit'.\""

msgid "He wasn't always like this.  Olwen came not long after we married, he was a great, caring father to her.  A few months before <the_cataclysm> is when he lost it, got in some survivalist circle.  He'd stay up pouring over newspapers and any documents he could find, and wound up quitting his job to study it more.  We didn't see much of him for a while, always in the basement, and took out a chunk of our savings to buy canned goods en masse."
msgstr "He wasn't always like this.  Olwen came not long after we married, he was a great, caring father to her.  A few months before <the_cataclysm> is when he lost it, got in some survivalist circle.  He'd stay up pouring over newspapers and any documents he could find, and wound up quitting his job to study it more.  We didn't see much of him for a while, always in the basement, and took out a chunk of our savings to buy tinned goods en masse."

msgid "We are all under God's protection here.  Our community, like all moral civilizations, has a set of rules.  Obey the Decalogue, have respect for your neighbors and we'll get along just fine, okay?"
msgstr "We are all under God's protection here.  Our community, like all moral civilisations, has a set of rules.  Obey the Decalogue, have respect for your neighbours and we'll get along just fine, okay?"

msgid "&Gemma is in deep, silent thought for a moment, before clearing her throat.  \"They read: 'I am the Lord your God, who brought you out of Egypt, out of the land of slavery.  You shall have no other gods before me.  You shall not make for yourself a carved image, or any likeness of anything that is in heaven above, or that is in the earth beneath, or that is in the water under the earth.  You shall not take the name of the Lord your God in vain.  Remember the Sabbath day, and keep it holy.  Honor your father and your mother.  You shall not murder.  You shall not commit adultery.  You shall not steal.  You shall not bear false witness against your neighbor.  You shall not covet your neighbors house.\"  They're written in Exodus 20:1-17, for future reference."
msgstr "&Gemma is in deep, silent thought for a moment, before clearing her throat.  \"They read: 'I am the Lord your God, who brought you out of Egypt, out of the land of slavery.  You shall have no other gods before me.  You shall not make for yourself a carved image, or any likeness of anything that is in heaven above, or that is in the earth beneath, or that is in the water under the earth.  You shall not take the name of the Lord your God in vain.  Remember the Sabbath day, and keep it holy.  Honour your father and your mother.  You shall not murder.  You shall not commit adultery.  You shall not steal.  You shall not bear false witness against your neighbour.  You shall not covet your neighbours house.\"  They're written in Exodus 20:1-17, for future reference."

msgid "I always have things on the go: tidying, organizing, cleaning, but I don't complain.  I never complain."
msgstr "I always have things on the go: tidying, organising, cleaning, but I don't complain.  I never complain."

msgid "I am a prophet, like my uncle before me.  He saw <the_cataclysm>, the righteous judgment of God and set about preparing an ark to save us.  He passed before his visions could be fulfilled, and now I carry his righteous banner."
msgstr "I am a prophet, like my uncle before me.  He saw <the_cataclysm>, the righteous judgement of God and set about preparing an ark to save us.  He passed before his visions could be fulfilled, and now I carry his righteous banner."

msgid "They denied us, they labeled us as a doomsday cult, threw sticks and stones at us, and yet, we were standing resiliently.  Why?  Because we knew God was on our side."
msgstr "They denied us, they labelled us as a doomsday cult, threw sticks and stones at us, and yet, we were standing resiliently.  Why?  Because we knew God was on our side."

msgid "We are all under God's protection here.  Our community, like all moral civilizations, has a set of rules.  Obey the Decalogue, have respect for your neighbors and we'll get along just fine.  Go see Gemma or Julian for a bed, if one's available.  We do have limited space on our Ark, though."
msgstr "We are all under God's protection here.  Our community, like all moral civilisations, has a set of rules.  Obey the Decalogue, have respect for your neighbours and we'll get along just fine.  Go see Gemma or Julian for a bed, if one's available.  We do have limited space on our Ark, though."

msgid "&Helena flips through her Bible before stopping.  \"They read: 'I am the Lord your God, who brought you out of Egypt, out of the land of slavery.  You shall have no other gods before me.  You shall not make for yourself a carved image, or any likeness of anything that is in heaven above, or that is in the earth beneath, or that is in the water under the earth.  You shall not take the name of the Lord your God in vain.  Remember the Sabbath day, and keep it holy.  Honor your father and your mother.  You shall not murder.  You shall not commit adultery.  You shall not steal.  You shall not bear false witness against your neighbor.  You shall not covet your neighbors house.\"  They're written in Exodus 20:1-17, for future reference."
msgstr "&Helena flips through her Bible before stopping.  \"They read: 'I am the Lord your God, who brought you out of Egypt, out of the land of slavery.  You shall have no other gods before me.  You shall not make for yourself a carved image, or any likeness of anything that is in heaven above, or that is in the earth beneath, or that is in the water under the earth.  You shall not take the name of the Lord your God in vain.  Remember the Sabbath day, and keep it holy.  Honour your father and your mother.  You shall not murder.  You shall not commit adultery.  You shall not steal.  You shall not bear false witness against your neighbour.  You shall not covet your neighbours house.\"  They're written in Exodus 20:1-17, for future reference."

msgid "Yes, I was just informed of that.  I also heard that she found a large group of people living out in an old evacuation center, who consider themselves merchants.  That would be a good place to resume our spread of the Truth, perhaps we could find others who were faithful before <the_cataclysm>."
msgstr "Yes, I was just informed of that.  I also heard that she found a large group of people living out in an old evacuation centre, who consider themselves merchants.  That would be a good place to resume our spread of the Truth, perhaps we could find others who were faithful before <the_cataclysm>."

msgid "I'm just a traveler, kid.  I won't be staying here for long."
msgstr "I'm just a traveller, kid.  I won't be staying here for long."

msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "You sure?  I mean, you've been traveling for a long time, haven't you?  Alright, it's your decision.  Let me know when you changed your mind."
msgstr "You sure?  I mean, you've been travelling for a long time, haven't you?  Alright, it's your decision.  Let me know when you changed your mind."

msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "You sure?  I mean, you've been traveling for a long time, haven't you?  Alright, it's your decision.  Let me know when you changed your mind."
msgstr "You sure?  I mean, you've been travelling for a long time, haven't you?  Alright, it's your decision.  Let me know when you changed your mind."

msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "You sure?  I mean, you've been traveling for a long time, haven't you?  Alright, it's your decision.  Let me know when you changed your mind."
msgstr "You sure?  I mean, you've been travelling for a long time, haven't you?  Alright, it's your decision.  Let me know when you changed your mind."

msgid "Well, I might as well be honest with you.  I ran mostly, ran like the devil was chasin' me.  I was at one of the police stations in town, when we were called out to handle a violent mob on the loose.  When we got there, the people were crazy, smashing and killing everything in their way.  They had these bloodshot eyes and a weird goo in their mouths.  We pulled out all the stops to handle them.  When tear gas wouldn't work, the chief told us to draw guns and kill them all.  We did…  There was so much blood…  That maneuver killed a lot of them, but not all.  One snuck up behind a lady who worked with us, tore a whole section of her spine out.  She never even had time to scream, just slumped over the cruiser door…  So I jumped post and ran, never looked back.  God, I can still hear the cries…"
msgstr "Well, I might as well be honest with you.  I ran mostly, ran like the devil was chasin' me.  I was at one of the police stations in town, when we were called out to handle a violent mob on the loose.  When we got there, the people were crazy, smashing and killing everything in their way.  They had these bloodshot eyes and a weird goo in their mouths.  We pulled out all the stops to handle them.  When tear gas wouldn't work, the chief told us to draw guns and kill them all.  We did…  There was so much blood…  That manoeuvre killed a lot of them, but not all.  One snuck up behind a lady who worked with us, tore a whole section of her spine out.  She never even had time to scream, just slumped over the cruiser door…  So I jumped post and ran, never looked back.  God, I can still hear the cries…"

msgid "It's been a struggle, trying to keep this bunch together.  Oh things could be better here, of course.  It could always be, but sometimes we don't even realize how good we have it here."
msgstr "It's been a struggle, trying to keep this bunch together.  Oh things could be better here, of course.  It could always be, but sometimes we don't even realise how good we have it here."

msgid "Our prayers were heard.  We knew the day was coming, so we prepared.  Our community stockpiled months' worth of canned goods, well enough until the chaos ends.  With the food we have left, we could live peacefully, but we foolishly didn't take extra people into consideration.  With so much at risk, I don't think we can afford more people.  Though I'm not the one who makes the decisions here, and it's probably for the better."
msgstr "Our prayers were heard.  We knew the day was coming, so we prepared.  Our community stockpiled months' worth of tinned goods, well enough until the chaos ends.  With the food we have left, we could live peacefully, but we foolishly didn't take extra people into consideration.  With so much at risk, I don't think we can afford more people.  Though I'm not the one who makes the decisions here, and it's probably for the better."

msgid "I worked for the Church, organized charities and filed paperwork.  That's how I met the Founder.  I did so much for everyone, yet they never noticed…"
msgstr "I worked for the Church, organised charities and filed paperwork.  That's how I met the Founder.  I did so much for everyone, yet they never noticed…"

msgid "Foraging is about recognizing the abundance that is around us all the time, not seeking out rare species."
msgstr "Foraging is about recognising the abundance that is around us all the time, not seeking out rare species."

msgid "Fuck you then, you judgmental <name_b>."
msgstr "Fuck you then, you judgemental <name_b>."

msgid "I arrived a bit later than everyone else, I was at my studio when <the_cataclysm> came.  Had to dodge a big horde of <zombies> on my way out of town, totaled my car, and hiked the rest of the way."
msgstr "I arrived a bit later than everyone else, I was at my studio when <the_cataclysm> came.  Had to dodge a big horde of <zombies> on my way out of town, totalled my car, and hiked the rest of the way."

msgid "I'll have a pair of pants."
msgstr "I'll have a pair of trousers."

msgid "I'll have a pair of leather pants."
msgstr "I'll have a pair of leather trousers."

msgid "I'll have a set of body armor."
msgstr "I'll have a set of body armour."

msgid "I ordered a pair of pants."
msgstr "I ordered a pair of trousers."

msgid "I ordered a pair of leather pants."
msgstr "I ordered a pair of leather trousers."

msgid "I ordered a set of body armor."
msgstr "I ordered a set of body armour."

msgid "I sure can!  For now, I can make t-shirts, pants, dresses, dusters, trench coats, backpacks, jackets, and a gambeson; if that's your thing."
msgstr "I sure can!  For now, I can make t-shirts, trousers, dresses, dusters, trench coats, backpacks, jackets, and a gambeson; if that's your thing."

msgid "T-shirts, pants, jackets, and dresses are four icons.  Dusters, trench coats, and backpacks are eight icons.  A gambeson is sixteen."
msgstr "T-shirts, trousers, jackets, and dresses are four icons.  Dusters, trench coats, and backpacks are eight icons.  A gambeson is sixteen."

msgid "T-shirts, pants, jackets, and dresses take me just a day.  Dusters, trench coats, and backpacks take four days, while a gambeson takes six days."
msgstr "T-shirts, trousers, jackets, and dresses take me just a day.  Dusters, trench coats, and backpacks take four days, while a gambeson takes six days."

msgid "But of course!  Right now, I can make a set of pouches, pants, cloaks, thicker jackets, or even a full set of body armor; it should be useful in your travels."
msgstr "But of course!  Right now, I can make a set of pouches, trousers, cloaks, thicker jackets, or even a full set of body armour; it should be useful in your travels."

msgid "Pouches and pants are eight icons.  Cloaks and thick jackets are twelve icons.  A set of body armor is twenty-four."
msgstr "Pouches and trousers are eight icons.  Cloaks and thick jackets are twelve icons.  A set of body armour is twenty-four."

msgid "Pouches and pants take me two days.  Cloaks and thick jackets take four days, while the set of body armor takes six days."
msgstr "Pouches and trousers take me two days.  Cloaks and thick jackets take four days, while the set of body armour takes six days."

msgid "I'm just a traveler."
msgstr "I'm just a traveller."

msgid "I'm just a curious traveler."
msgstr "I'm just a curious traveller."

msgid "Not many travelers come through here these days.  There's not much left to wander too, besides a horde of <zombies>."
msgstr "Not many travellers come through here these days.  There's not much left to wander too, besides a horde of <zombies>."

msgid "Not many travelers come through here these days.  There's not much left to wander too, besides a horde of <zombies>.  The people here won't be too friendly with you either, so that sucks."
msgstr "Not many travellers come through here these days.  There's not much left to wander too, besides a horde of <zombies>.  The people here won't be too friendly with you either, so that sucks."

msgid "They're alright, I suppose.  Helena's an asshole as usual, we're low on supplies, and all scared to go twenty feet outside the gate."
msgstr "They're alright, I suppose.  Helena's an arsehole as usual, we're low on supplies, and all scared to go twenty feet outside the gate."

msgid "I'm just a curious traveler.  What's up with you?"
msgstr "I'm just a curious traveller.  What's up with you?"

msgid "Well, let's just say I'm interested in rare game.  I've heard stories, rumors and some tall tales about otherworldly beings out there in the wasteland.  That's where you come in.  I want to see the evidence, something physical I can collect as a trophy collection.  You seem to have experience, I was hoping you could help me."
msgstr "Well, let's just say I'm interested in rare game.  I've heard stories, rumours and some tall tales about otherworldly beings out there in the wasteland.  That's where you come in.  I want to see the evidence, something physical I can collect as a trophy collection.  You seem to have experience, I was hoping you could help me."

msgid "&Russel's expression becomes somber, and he briefly stares at the wall.  \"She was my dog, had her for seventeen years.  We used to go duck-hunting, she'd swim out and get anything I shot.  She helped me track many a deer through the woods…   When <the_cataclysm> hit, she saved me from some <zombies> when we were skippin' town, but she died…  Then she came back, wasn't herself…  I had to put her down.\""
msgstr "&Russel's expression becomes sombre, and he briefly stares at the wall.  \"She was my dog, had her for seventeen years.  We used to go duck-hunting, she'd swim out and get anything I shot.  She helped me track many a deer through the woods…   When <the_cataclysm> hit, she saved me from some <zombies> when we were skippin' town, but she died…  Then she came back, wasn't herself…  I had to put her down.\""

msgid "I'm just a curious traveler.  What about you, how are you doing?"
msgstr "I'm just a curious traveller.  What about you, how are you doing?"

msgid "Of course!  Just put all your literary findings on that chair over there.  Remember, you're not only doing a favor for me, but for all of humanity as well.  World heritage is what we're talking about!  I managed to get my hands on a book called 'Zombie Survival Guide' while, uh… dumpster diving.  Imagine how much this book alone reveals about our pre-Cataclysm culture!  Oh boy, how wrong we were about everything."
msgstr "Of course!  Just put all your literary findings on that chair over there.  Remember, you're not only doing a favour for me, but for all of humanity as well.  World heritage is what we're talking about!  I managed to get my hands on a book called 'Zombie Survival Guide' while, uh… skip diving.  Imagine how much this book alone reveals about our pre-Cataclysm culture!  Oh boy, how wrong we were about everything."

msgid "She's my wife, worked for the Church before <the_cataclysm>.  She used to organize charities for the needy, now we're the ones in need of charity.  She has a bit of a high horse these days, but a nice lady once you get to know her.  We've been married for 28 years, and I couldn't ask for a better wife."
msgstr "She's my wife, worked for the Church before <the_cataclysm>.  She used to organise charities for the needy, now we're the ones in need of charity.  She has a bit of a high horse these days, but a nice lady once you get to know her.  We've been married for 28 years, and I couldn't ask for a better wife."

msgid "I really like to draw things, I primarily did landscapes in my spare time.  I like paper-and-pencil sketches, but I have worked with watercolors and oil canvases.  Never could get my head around the digital stuff, though, too complex for me and I never had a good free hand with a stylus.  I also shot a bit, went hunting a few times.  I mainly went to the gun range though, shotguns were always my forte.  Besides that, I watched some TV and regular ol' stuff.  I also like to read quite a bit, too."
msgstr "I really like to draw things, I primarily did landscapes in my spare time.  I like paper-and-pencil sketches, but I have worked with watercolours and oil canvases.  Never could get my head around the digital stuff, though, too complex for me and I never had a good free hand with a stylus.  I also shot a bit, went hunting a few times.  I mainly went to the gun range though, shotguns were always my forte.  Besides that, I watched some TV and regular ol' stuff.  I also like to read quite a bit, too."

msgid "I don't know anymore, to tell you the truth.  I was planning on settling down and having kids, but now that everyone's dead and the judgment of God has come to pass, I'll seek His truth and try to keep on living.  One day, when this is all over, I'll fly away to Heaven's pearly gates and be with the angels.  As for the Earth, I'd rather not think about the things that have come to pass."
msgstr "I don't know anymore, to tell you the truth.  I was planning on settling down and having kids, but now that everyone's dead and the judgement of God has come to pass, I'll seek His truth and try to keep on living.  One day, when this is all over, I'll fly away to Heaven's pearly gates and be with the angels.  As for the Earth, I'd rather not think about the things that have come to pass."

msgid "Sure, I'd be willing to purchase some.  I'll have to work up the money with Helena, but I'm sure we've got it.  I'd prefer canned, and preserved goods.  How much are you talkin'?"
msgstr "Sure, I'd be willing to purchase some.  I'll have to work up the money with Helena, but I'm sure we've got it.  I'd prefer tinned, and preserved goods.  How much are you talkin'?"

msgid "I'll just take them as is, thanks.  Everything can be finalized later."
msgstr "I'll just take them as is, thanks.  Everything can be finalised later."

msgid "Well well well, another traveler.  Don't try anything suspicious, you're outnumbered here and we're well armed, and my boss will know what happens soon enough."
msgstr "Well well well, another traveller.  Don't try anything suspicious, you're outnumbered here and we're well armed, and my boss will know what happens soon enough."

msgid "No offense, but my clients definitely would not like me giving strangers directions to their hideouts.  You'll have to find them on their own terms."
msgstr "No offence, but my clients definitely would not like me giving strangers directions to their hideouts.  You'll have to find them on their own terms."

msgid "A traveler brought this to me in return for some rabbits.  Said that he'd gotten it from a scientist out in the swamps but it took up too much space in his car."
msgstr "A traveller brought this to me in return for some rabbits.  Said that he'd gotten it from a scientist out in the swamps but it took up too much space in his car."

msgid "You do realize there is an apocalypse going on, right?"
msgstr "You do realise there is an apocalypse going on, right?"

msgid "Hah, real cute.  Seem the End times didn't take your sense of humor, eh, stranger?"
msgstr "Hah, real cute.  Seem the End times didn't take your sense of humour, eh, stranger?"

msgid "What?\"  The naked, traumatized man stares at you blankly, as though he'd never seen Star Wars, which is clearly ridiculous.  \"Rescue me?  Yes, oh please yes!"
msgstr "What?\"  The naked, traumatised man stares at you blankly, as though he'd never seen Star Wars, which is clearly ridiculous.  \"Rescue me?  Yes, oh please yes!"

msgid "Fair enough, you asked for it.\"  He stretches his arms out.  \"Jack and I stayed close, even after my old man and I fell out, so when it looked like he was going to be saddled with the entire farm to run, I took a good long look at my life and realized I hated it.  It was never the farm I was trying to get away from, you know?  I packed up my things, quit my job, and came out to help Jack.  Never looked back.\"  He chuckles.  \"Damn hard finding a partner for a guy like me out here though.  I was in a long-term relationship when I left, but that fell apart.  I haven't been too lonely though, I've got my people."
msgstr "Fair enough, you asked for it.\"  He stretches his arms out.  \"Jack and I stayed close, even after my old man and I fell out, so when it looked like he was going to be saddled with the entire farm to run, I took a good long look at my life and realised I hated it.  It was never the farm I was trying to get away from, you know?  I packed up my things, quit my job, and came out to help Jack.  Never looked back.\"  He chuckles.  \"Damn hard finding a partner for a guy like me out here though.  I was in a long-term relationship when I left, but that fell apart.  I haven't been too lonely though, I've got my people."

msgid "Look, I took it off to show I'm not here as a marshal.  I'm just here as a traveler, someone who can maybe help you out.  I know you've got problems bigger than you can handle right now."
msgstr "Look, I took it off to show I'm not here as a marshal.  I'm just here as a traveller, someone who can maybe help you out.  I know you've got problems bigger than you can handle right now."

msgid "Chris is hiking the perimeter of our land, planning some defense options.\"  He looks you up and down.  \"Best just let him be."
msgstr "Chris is hiking the perimeter of our land, planning some defence options.\"  He looks you up and down.  \"Best just let him be."

msgid "I appreciate it, this will really make a difference, here's some horse armor I've been working on.  Eventually I'll have the whole herd outfitted."
msgstr "I appreciate it, this will really make a difference, here's some horse armour I've been working on.  Eventually I'll have the whole herd outfitted."

msgid "Thanks, I was getting ready to go look myself.  Now that I have the anvil, I've been working on new armor for the horses, take this prototype I made."
msgstr "Thanks, I was getting ready to go look myself.  Now that I have the anvil, I've been working on new armour for the horses, take this prototype I made."

msgid "I'm a bit worried about defenses.  Do you folks have any armor or equipment to help keep yourselves safe?"
msgstr "I'm a bit worried about defences.  Do you folks have any armour or equipment to help keep yourselves safe?"

msgid "I think you're right, that would take too long.  We'll have to count on offense being our best defense."
msgstr "I think you're right, that would take too long.  We'll have to count on offence being our best defence."

msgid "[5 Riot Armor] I've got enough riot armor for everyone."
msgstr "[5 Riot Armour] I've got enough riot armour for everyone."

msgid "We have enough full sets of riot control armor to cover everyone, head to toe."
msgstr "We have enough full sets of riot control armour to cover everyone, head to toe."

msgid "Retrieve 5 sets of riot armor for the Isherwoods"
msgstr "Retrieve 5 sets of riot armour for the Isherwoods"

msgid "Some of their cows were killed before we realized what was happening, Barry and Carlos went into the forest to find the predator but it was like nothing they'd ever seen.  Carlos may be willing to tell you more."
msgstr "Some of their cows were killed before we realised what was happening, Barry and Carlos went into the forest to find the predator but it was like nothing they'd ever seen.  Carlos may be willing to tell you more."

msgid "*is a sun-worn, middle-aged man with crows feet and graying hair.  He looks up as you approach, "
msgstr "*is a sun-worn, middle-aged man with crows feet and greying hair.  He looks up as you approach, "

msgid "<color_green>[Social 3]</color> I swear, I'm not here to cause trouble.  I just volunteer with those guys to help travelers, things like that.  I don't speak for them."
msgstr "<color_green>[Social 3]</color> I swear, I'm not here to cause trouble.  I just volunteer with those guys to help travellers, things like that.  I don't speak for them."

msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Hello traveler, what brings you here?"
msgstr "Hello traveller, what brings you here?"

msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "Hello traveler, what brings you here?"
msgstr "Hello traveller, what brings you here?"

msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "Hello traveler, what brings you here?"
msgstr "Hello traveller, what brings you here?"

msgid "Even out here we've had some attacks and seen… other things.  We have been working on our defenses, but it takes time.  We've been able to keep up with the crops and animals though so we won't have to risk our necks for supplies."
msgstr "Even out here we've had some attacks and seen… other things.  We have been working on our defences, but it takes time.  We've been able to keep up with the crops and animals though so we won't have to risk our necks for supplies."

msgid "What sort of defenses do you want?"
msgstr "What sort of defences do you want?"

msgid "We could use some 3 liter jars to preserve our produce.  Can you bring me 10 large three liter jars?  I'll give you some preserves in exchange."
msgstr "We could use some 3 litre jars to preserve our produce.  Can you bring me 10 large three litre jars?  I'll give you some preserves in exchange."

msgid "Sounds like you are betting on civilization not coming back."
msgstr "Sounds like you are betting on civilisation not coming back."

msgid "He's out doing some surveying, we are planning on adding a fence line and some defenses."
msgstr "He's out doing some surveying, we are planning on adding a fence line and some defences."

msgid "I appreciate it, this will help keep our animals safe.  This is, Steve, he's a good, steady horse.  You should talk to Carlos about some armor for him."
msgstr "I appreciate it, this will help keep our animals safe.  This is, Steve, he's a good, steady horse.  You should talk to Carlos about some armour for him."

msgid "What's with all the weapons and armor?"
msgstr "What's with all the weapons and armour?"

msgid "Could you make me a suit of armor?"
msgstr "Could you make me a suit of armour?"

msgid "How is my armor coming?"
msgstr "How is my armour coming?"

msgid "I make them myself!  I've always loved traditional armaments and am a proud member of the SCA!  Figured now that everything has gone to hell I can make it a full-time thing.  Lots of survivors in need of a big ol' hammer or some armored guards to keep the biters off."
msgstr "I make them myself!  I've always loved traditional armaments and am a proud member of the SCA!  Figured now that everything has gone to hell I can make it a full-time thing.  Lots of survivors in need of a big ol' hammer or some armoured guards to keep the biters off."

msgid "Well, not *anyone*, but I've always been a believer in community.  The shop is run as a co-op, so if you want access you'll have to buy a share.  As a partial owner, you will have full access to the shop.  Shares are currently 100 merch; I hate the currency but it's the closest thing we've got to a representation of labor."
msgstr "Well, not *anyone*, but I've always been a believer in community.  The shop is run as a co-op, so if you want access you'll have to buy a share.  As a partial owner, you will have full access to the shop.  Shares are currently 100 merch; I hate the currency but it's the closest thing we've got to a representation of labour."

msgid "Have you apologized?"
msgstr "Have you apologised?"

msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Sure.  After what you did for me, I'd equip an army for you.  I'll need some money to negotiate with the caravans and scavengers that come by.  What level of protection are you thinking?  I can do 2mm, 4mm, and 6mm suits depending on how much you want to resemble a tank, or I can make you a suit of chainmail instead if you want a little more flexibility.  Materials costs are 300 merch to pay for the food I need to do the labor plus 100 merch per 2mm or 50 merch for the chainmail.  Whatever I save in non-scaling bits like the chain and leather, I get gouged in looking for so much bulk metal."
msgstr "Sure.  After what you did for me, I'd equip an army for you.  I'll need some money to negotiate with the caravans and scavengers that come by.  What level of protection are you thinking?  I can do 2mm, 4mm, and 6mm suits depending on how much you want to resemble a tank, or I can make you a suit of chainmail instead if you want a little more flexibility.  Materials costs are 300 merch to pay for the food I need to do the labour plus 100 merch per 2mm or 50 merch for the chainmail.  Whatever I save in non-scaling bits like the chain and leather, I get gouged in looking for so much bulk metal."

msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "Sure.  After what you did for me, I'd equip an army for you.  I'll need some money to negotiate with the caravans and scavengers that come by.  What level of protection are you thinking?  I can do 2mm, 4mm, and 6mm suits depending on how much you want to resemble a tank, or I can make you a suit of chainmail instead if you want a little more flexibility.  Materials costs are 300 merch to pay for the food I need to do the labor plus 100 merch per 2mm or 50 merch for the chainmail.  Whatever I save in non-scaling bits like the chain and leather, I get gouged in looking for so much bulk metal."
