msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Well well, another traveler.  Don't try anything, you're outnumbered here and we're well armed."
msgstr "Well well, another traveller.  Don't try anything, you're outnumbered here and we're well armed."

msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "Well well, another traveler.  Don't try anything, you're outnumbered here and we're well armed."
msgstr "Well well, another traveller.  Don't try anything, you're outnumbered here and we're well armed."

msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "Well well, another traveler.  Don't try anything, you're outnumbered here and we're well armed."
msgstr "Well well, another traveller.  Don't try anything, you're outnumbered here and we're well armed."

msgid "We're just travelers, making a pit stop.  Might be willing to trade a bit, if you've got anything to share.  We're not looking for trouble, there's plenty of that on the roads already."
msgstr "We're just travellers, making a pit stop.  Might be willing to trade a bit, if you've got anything to share.  We're not looking for trouble, there's plenty of that on the roads already."

msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "No offense, but my clients definitely would not like me giving strangers directions to their hideouts.  You'll have to find them on their own terms."
msgstr "No offence, but my clients definitely would not like me giving strangers directions to their hideouts.  You'll have to find them on their own terms."

msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "No offense, but my clients definitely would not like me giving strangers directions to their hideouts.  You'll have to find them on their own terms."
msgstr "No offence, but my clients definitely would not like me giving strangers directions to their hideouts.  You'll have to find them on their own terms."

msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "No offense, but my clients definitely would not like me giving strangers directions to their hideouts.  You'll have to find them on their own terms."
msgstr "No offence, but my clients definitely would not like me giving strangers directions to their hideouts.  You'll have to find them on their own terms."

msgid "*glances your way, then makes eye contact as you move closer to speak.  He is a strong-looking man in his mid forties, his hair graying and his face flecked with stubble and travel dust.  The clothes he's wearing are clearly scavenged, though they fit well, and he has the build of someone who until recently had the luxury of carrying a few extra pounds.  \"Hi there.\"  He presents his hand to shake.  \"You don't look like you belong here.  Name's Bailey, John Bailey.\""
msgstr "*glances your way, then makes eye contact as you move closer to speak.  He is a strong-looking man in his mid forties, his hair greying and his face flecked with stubble and travel dust.  The clothes he's wearing are clearly scavenged, though they fit well, and he has the build of someone who until recently had the luxury of carrying a few extra pounds.  \"Hi there.\"  He presents his hand to shake.  \"You don't look like you belong here.  Name's Bailey, John Bailey.\""

msgid "I don't really know.  Food stocks aren't too bad for me and mine, I found a stock of canned goods early on that will last us for a while yet.  I don't use a gun if I can avoid it, too noisy.  I notice these guys seem to keep a lot of building supplies though, and trying to get a vehicle downtown to loot a hardware store or a lumberyard is suicide, so I think that's where they're going to get my money.  I wonder if they deliver."
msgstr "I don't really know.  Food stocks aren't too bad for me and mine, I found a stock of tinned goods early on that will last us for a while yet.  I don't use a gun if I can avoid it, too noisy.  I notice these guys seem to keep a lot of building supplies though, and trying to get a vehicle downtown to loot a hardware store or a lumberyard is suicide, so I think that's where they're going to get my money.  I wonder if they deliver."

msgid "Yeah, I, uh… I know a bit about that stuff.  Hard not to empathize, especially when I know I'm not quite as hard as others, by sheer luck.  Besides, there are so few of us left now.  What's the point in wasting time judging other people for how hard they took the end of the world?"
msgstr "Yeah, I, uh… I know a bit about that stuff.  Hard not to empathise, especially when I know I'm not quite as hard as others, by sheer luck.  Besides, there are so few of us left now.  What's the point in wasting time judging other people for how hard they took the end of the world?"

msgid "*rubs his stubble, looking thoughtful.  \"I agree it's important to be independent, but don't forget, working together is what makes us better than the undead.  It's how we got out of the trees and fields, and into civilization.  Anyway, I don't want to talk philosophy at you.  If you're doing well on your own, more power to you!\""
msgstr "*rubs his stubble, looking thoughtful.  \"I agree it's important to be independent, but don't forget, working together is what makes us better than the undead.  It's how we got out of the trees and fields, and into civilisation.  Anyway, I don't want to talk philosophy at you.  If you're doing well on your own, more power to you!\""

msgid "Sure, I guess.  I don't know if I know anything you don't, you seem like you can handle yourself.  I've made it this far by not engaging whenever possible.  I'm never going to kill all the zombies out there.  Darius and I try not to fight if we can avoid it, and if we can't, we try to always have the advantage.  Numbers, weaponry, terrain.  Zombies are clumsy and stupid so we lead them across bushes and things to trip and stumble.  We take high ground and let them plough into ladders like idiots while we stick 'em with spears from above.  Mostly, though, we try not to be seen.  We use bikes instead of cars because they don't make noise and don't need gas, plus we can take forest trails and things and avoid traffic jams.  Those things are suicide.  We try to avoid the cities, and when we do go close, we stick to the outskirts and raid the outlying houses.  In those, we keep crouched and try to get deep into the building fast, or down into the basement, so that little noises don't carry much and nothing from outside can see us.  Also, zombies being idiots, closing the blinds is a great move.  I always keep a crowbar for opening doors and windows, but I try not to use it if I can avoid it.  Darius can pick locks, which is slower but doesn't make noise.  We get a lot more mileage from raiding gas stations and other rural sites, where if there are a few zombies, we can usually lead them away."
msgstr "Sure, I guess.  I don't know if I know anything you don't, you seem like you can handle yourself.  I've made it this far by not engaging whenever possible.  I'm never going to kill all the zombies out there.  Darius and I try not to fight if we can avoid it, and if we can't, we try to always have the advantage.  Numbers, weaponry, terrain.  Zombies are clumsy and stupid so we lead them across bushes and things to trip and stumble.  We take high ground and let them plough into ladders like idiots while we stick 'em with spears from above.  Mostly, though, we try not to be seen.  We use bikes instead of cars because they don't make noise and don't need gas, plus we can take forest trails and things and avoid traffic jams.  Those things are suicide.  We try to avoid the cities, and when we do go close, we stick to the outskirts and raid the outlying houses.  In those, we keep crouched and try to get deep into the building fast, or down into the basement, so that little noises don't carry much and nothing from outside can see us.  Also, zombies being idiots, closing the blinds is a great move.  I always keep a crowbar for opening doors and windows, but I try not to use it if I can avoid it.  Darius can pick locks, which is slower but doesn't make noise.  We get a lot more mileage from raiding petrol stations and other rural sites, where if there are a few zombies, we can usually lead them away."

msgid "We were at the same little evacuation hut, but it was all messed up, just used condoms and broken bottles and lipstick writing on the walls.  We found another group of refugees like us on the road, but they had all been killed, all ripped up, blood everywhere.  We took their food and made it all the way to a big refugee center, but somebody there with a gun told us there was no room, so we're going to a FEMA camp.  They should have more room and supplies.  No guarantees, but it's a chance."
msgstr "We were at the same little evacuation hut, but it was all messed up, just used condoms and broken bottles and lipstick writing on the walls.  We found another group of refugees like us on the road, but they had all been killed, all ripped up, blood everywhere.  We took their food and made it all the way to a big refugee centre, but somebody there with a gun told us there was no room, so we're going to a FEMA camp.  They should have more room and supplies.  No guarantees, but it's a chance."

msgid "I haven't been to any refugee center.  Can you tell me where it is?"
msgstr "I haven't been to any refugee centre.  Can you tell me where it is?"

msgid "Reach Refugee Center"
msgstr "Reach Refugee Centre"

msgid "This beggar in the refugee center has had something to eat recently."
msgstr "This beggar in the refugee centre has had something to eat recently."

msgid "Out there?  That's suicide!  People that go out there don't come back, people who can hold their own… unlike me.  I'd rather take my chances begging for scraps and waiting for someone in the center to die and make room for me, thanks."
msgstr "Out there?  That's suicide!  People that go out there don't come back, people who can hold their own… unlike me.  I'd rather take my chances begging for scraps and waiting for someone in the centre to die and make room for me, thanks."

msgid "That's quite the offer, but I don't think I'd survive the trip.  I don't think you realize how useless I am in this world."
msgstr "That's quite the offer, but I don't think I'd survive the trip.  I don't think you realise how useless I am in this world."

msgid "There's so much of it now, and the zombies are afraid of it.  It's kept me safe so far.  The beta rays come from the center point of the zombie, so it hits the cardboard and can't penetrate.  The reflection can stop any further damage."
msgstr "There's so much of it now, and the zombies are afraid of it.  It's kept me safe so far.  The beta rays come from the centre point of the zombie, so it hits the cardboard and can't penetrate.  The reflection can stop any further damage."

msgid "Sure, Dave.  One last favor, I think I can talk to Smokes about finding you a place to go."
msgstr "Sure, Dave.  One last favour, I think I can talk to Smokes about finding you a place to go."

msgid "Well, OK then, Dave.  One last favor, I think I can talk to Smokes about finding you a place to go."
msgstr "Well, OK then, Dave.  One last favour, I think I can talk to Smokes about finding you a place to go."

msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Look, I'm sorry for freaking out earlier.  You might be an asshole but I'm sure you didn't mean it like that.  My blood sugar is hella low, I get a bit cranky.  We cool?"
msgstr "Look, I'm sorry for freaking out earlier.  You might be an arsehole but I'm sure you didn't mean it like that.  My blood sugar is hella low, I get a bit cranky.  We cool?"

