msgid "The mercenary's demeanor changes completely when they realize you aren't here to waste time.  \"Alright, tell you what.  Get me twelve coins and that's giving my skills away, just anything to be done with that voice on a box.\""
msgstr "The mercenary's demeanour changes completely when they realise you aren't here to waste time.  \"Alright, tell you what.  Get me twelve coins and that's giving my skills away, just anything to be done with that voice on a box.\""

msgid "A traumatized mercenary has claimed to have seen what you assume to be a powerful monster.  Maybe you should investigate this for the benefit of everyone."
msgstr "A traumatised mercenary has claimed to have seen what you assume to be a powerful monster.  Maybe you should investigate this for the benefit of everyone."

msgid "&You see one more traumatized face, all too many and too frequent for any help to be worthwhile."
msgstr "&You see one more traumatised face, all too many and too frequent for any help to be worthwhile."

msgid "Leave the traveler to their trauma."
msgstr "Leave the traveller to their trauma."

msgid "the traumatized traveler"
msgstr "the traumatised traveller"

msgid "Oh, hey.  The rumors were true, there really is someone new around.  Nice to meet you, call me Darla."
msgstr "Oh, hey.  The rumours were true, there really is someone new around.  Nice to meet you, call me Darla."

msgid "Oooh, the NEW person.  So, you're not just some rumor they cooked up as a team building exercise.  I'm Sunil, welcome to the underground."
msgstr "Oooh, the NEW person.  So, you're not just some rumour they cooked up as a team building exercise.  I'm Sunil, welcome to the underground."

msgid "&An intercom is embedded into the wall here, just next to the card reader.  It's a metal box about as big as a dinner plate, with a speaker shaped like a downwards curve and a large camera prominently featured in the center.  You see a single metal button with a dark LED next to it.  The intercom is silent."
msgstr "&An intercom is embedded into the wall here, just next to the card reader.  It's a metal box about as big as a dinner plate, with a speaker shaped like a downwards curve and a large camera prominently featured in the centre.  You see a single metal button with a dark LED next to it.  The intercom is silent."

msgid "How's that armor working?"
msgstr "How's that armour working?"

msgid "The traders at the refugee center asked me to deliver this drive of FEMA data…"
msgstr "The traders at the refugee centre asked me to deliver this drive of FEMA data…"

msgid "Your scientist was wearing some kind of armor.  What is it?"
msgstr "Your scientist was wearing some kind of armour.  What is it?"

msgid "I saw that your mercs have specialty rifles.  Would I be able to get one of those?"
msgstr "I saw that your mercs have speciality rifles.  Would I be able to get one of those?"

msgid "I need some gear to outfit my crew, I think five sets of police riot armor would do the trick."
msgstr "I need some gear to outfit my crew, I think five sets of police riot armour would do the trick."

msgid "Cost of the armor plus everything left in the tower."
msgstr "Cost of the armour plus everything left in the tower."

msgid "&The intercom crackles with static as it turns on.  The LED next to the button lights up a bright red, and the camera lens whirs as it focuses on you.  There is no immediate response."
msgstr "&The intercom crackles with static as it turns on.  The LED next to the button lights up a bright red, and the camera lens whirrs as it focuses on you.  There is no immediate response."

msgid "The merchant at the refugee center sent me.  You were looking for a hard drive from them?"
msgstr "The merchant at the refugee centre sent me.  You were looking for a hard drive from them?"

msgid "You do realize that the front door is just open?"
msgstr "You do realise that the front door is just open?"

msgid "Certainly.  I've just finished speaking with a certain individual, who has authorized you limited access to a selection of our internal stores.  We will provide you with pay for contracts in the form of tokens to be used as an exchange currency, which you can then trade for goods.  We are also amenable to bartering in exchange for supplies that are currently difficult for us to obtain from outside the facility."
msgstr "Certainly.  I've just finished speaking with a certain individual, who has authorised you limited access to a selection of our internal stores.  We will provide you with pay for contracts in the form of tokens to be used as an exchange currency, which you can then trade for goods.  We are also amenable to bartering in exchange for supplies that are currently difficult for us to obtain from outside the facility."

msgid "Yes and no.  When something like this is going on, the storm is going to affect you one way or another, but being outside is much more dangerous.  If you can, find a solid shelter.  Stay as far away from the outer walls as you can.  Being underground is probably a good idea.  There are likely undocumented psychological effects; use your best judgment and your common sense."
msgstr "Yes and no.  When something like this is going on, the storm is going to affect you one way or another, but being outside is much more dangerous.  If you can, find a solid shelter.  Stay as far away from the outer walls as you can.  Being underground is probably a good idea.  There are likely undocumented psychological effects; use your best judgement and your common sense."

msgid ""
"Potentially.  We recently came into possession of a video taken during the first days of <the_cataclysm> using a home camcorder.  We have ruled out possible tampering, and conclude that the recording is legitimate.  It depicts an entity that appeared to rapidly change shape, but responded especially strongly to human presence.  Eventually, the entity reshaped itself into a small object, which the author of the recording claimed had anomalous properties.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Subsequent entities of this type have failed to manifest during remote observation of the phenomenon.  We hypothesize that, if they do exist at all, they may only appear in response to human presence.  While we consider the hypothesis too dangerous and too uncertain to test using our own resources, we would be eager to hear the results if you attempted to do so yourself."
msgstr ""
"Potentially.  We recently came into possession of a video taken during the first days of <the_cataclysm> using a home camcorder.  We have ruled out possible tampering, and conclude that the recording is legitimate.  It depicts an entity that appeared to rapidly change shape, but responded especially strongly to human presence.  Eventually, the entity reshaped itself into a small object, which the author of the recording claimed had anomalous properties.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Subsequent entities of this type have failed to manifest during remote observation of the phenomenon.  We hypothesise that, if they do exist at all, they may only appear in response to human presence.  While we consider the hypothesis too dangerous and too uncertain to test using our own resources, we would be eager to hear the results if you attempted to do so yourself."

msgid "We've been working on specialized gear for potential agents in the field, given the hardware we have available.  Given the risks we've observed from here, it seemed astute.  It seems we still have some work to do."
msgstr "We've been working on specialised gear for potential agents in the field, given the hardware we have available.  Given the risks we've observed from here, it seemed astute.  It seems we still have some work to do."

msgid "[INT 10] The pieces seemed warped.  Whatever you're using to reinforce the armor isn't strong enough."
msgstr "[INT 10] The pieces seemed warped.  Whatever you're using to reinforce the armour isn't strong enough."

msgid "&The intercom goes quiet for a moment.  You hear a brief exchange on the other end, and then the microphone squeals as the voice gets closer again.  \"As additional payment for helping resolve the situation, feel free to keep the modular defense system.  The core armor platform is solid, and we have been iterating on supplementary pieces that we would be willing to trade to you.\""
msgstr "&The intercom goes quiet for a moment.  You hear a brief exchange on the other end, and then the microphone squeals as the voice gets closer again.  \"As additional payment for helping resolve the situation, feel free to keep the modular defence system.  The core armour platform is solid, and we have been iterating on supplementary pieces that we would be willing to trade to you.\""

msgid "We've solved that issue with our more recent prototypes.\"  There is a brief pause.  \"You seem like a good candidate.  We will transfer over the additional pieces to complete that prototype set, with the goal of collecting additional field data.  The core armor platform is solid, and we have been iterating on supplementary pieces we would be willing to trade to you.  Any feedback on their performance would be appreciated."
msgstr "We've solved that issue with our more recent prototypes.\"  There is a brief pause.  \"You seem like a good candidate.  We will transfer over the additional pieces to complete that prototype set, with the goal of collecting additional field data.  The core armour platform is solid, and we have been iterating on supplementary pieces we would be willing to trade to you.  Any feedback on their performance would be appreciated."

msgid "It's built with experimental combat programming and some heavy-duty armor.  Despite the armor, it's pretty nimble, so unless you've got a vehicle don't expect to outrun it.  We decided to hold off on adding long-range weapons until we finished the initial field testing, so if you can keep your distance, you should be safe."
msgstr "It's built with experimental combat programming and some heavy-duty armour.  Despite the armour, it's pretty nimble, so unless you've got a vehicle don't expect to outrun it.  We decided to hold off on adding long-range weapons until we finished the initial field testing, so if you can keep your distance, you should be safe."

msgid "To be specific, there have been anomalous readings that we are unable to explain.  Seismic disturbances have been recorded emanating from the ruins, with a magnitude ranging from two to four, and periodic vocalizations have been documented to exceed 150 decibels.  We are uncertain why or how these phenomena are created."
msgstr "To be specific, there have been anomalous readings that we are unable to explain.  Seismic disturbances have been recorded emanating from the ruins, with a magnitude ranging from two to four, and periodic vocalisations have been documented to exceed 150 decibels.  We are uncertain why or how these phenomena are created."

msgid "Excellent.  Thank you very much.\"  The intercom recites a series of coordinates.  \"Exercise a great deal of caution.  We do not know what the conditions on the ground are like.  Use your best judgment.  As before, we are willing to offer you protective gear, if you would like it."
msgstr "Excellent.  Thank you very much.\"  The intercom recites a series of coordinates.  \"Exercise a great deal of caution.  We do not know what the conditions on the ground are like.  Use your best judgement.  As before, we are willing to offer you protective gear, if you would like it."

msgid ""
"One of our scout drones spotted a partially-malfunctioning robot of unconventional make while tracking an anomalous radiation spike close by.  We project that much knowledge could be gained from a close examination of this subject, and you would be tasked to retrieve it for us intact.  We will equip you with a prototype rifle and instructions on how to use it and deactivate the robot, if you accept.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"The success of this contract requires that the subject be brought back in an inactive state, and *not* destroyed.  A ruined robot is of no scientific value.  We emphasize that you use the prototype to complete this task; an EMP blast would likely destroy the subject outright.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Completion of this contract awards 2 HGC, and you will be able to keep the prototype and the equipment used to operate it."
msgstr ""
"One of our scout drones spotted a partially-malfunctioning robot of unconventional make while tracking an anomalous radiation spike close by.  We project that much knowledge could be gained from a close examination of this subject, and you would be tasked to retrieve it for us intact.  We will equip you with a prototype rifle and instructions on how to use it and deactivate the robot, if you accept.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"The success of this contract requires that the subject be brought back in an inactive state, and *not* destroyed.  A ruined robot is of no scientific value.  We emphasise that you use the prototype to complete this task; an EMP blast would likely destroy the subject outright.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Completion of this contract awards 2 HGC, and you will be able to keep the prototype and the equipment used to operate it."

msgid "We are as of yet uncertain of its origin and purpose.  Its body most closely resembles a pyramid on what we believe are three sets of legs for mobility.  It is lightly armed, and has attacked our cam-spy drones using high-voltage electric discharge.  We theorize that this is most likely for deterrence, and not to cause direct harm.  Nonetheless, we need to emphasize that its full capabilities are unknown, and we do not know how it will react when confronted with a living threat."
msgstr "We are as of yet uncertain of its origin and purpose.  Its body most closely resembles a pyramid on what we believe are three sets of legs for mobility.  It is lightly armed, and has attacked our cam-spy drones using high-voltage electric discharge.  We theorise that this is most likely for deterrence, and not to cause direct harm.  Nonetheless, we need to emphasise that its full capabilities are unknown, and we do not know how it will react when confronted with a living threat."

msgid "We believe so; it underwent intensive internal tests on existing and theoretical models before giving it to you.  UGVs, autonomous CROWS units, manhacks, and other robots should all be possible to neutralize by using the weapon, although we advise great caution; the weapon is short-ranged, and was not designed to target distant enemies."
msgstr "We believe so; it underwent intensive internal tests on existing and theoretical models before giving it to you.  UGVs, autonomous CROWS units, manhacks, and other robots should all be possible to neutralise by using the weapon, although we advise great caution; the weapon is short-ranged, and was not designed to target distant enemies."

msgid ""
"During the Cataclysm, we lost contact with one of our sister sites, LIXA.  Aerial surveillance indicates that the facility's inhabitants are deceased, and beyond the now-zombified security detail, the site should be sparsely populated.  We want you to enter the facility and make a copy of what they were researching on the provided thumb drive.  Additionally, we will be providing you with a keycard that should at the very least get you in the front door.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We're offering a standard 5 HGC for successful retrieval of the data.  If that isn't enough of an incentive, we do have a manifest from before we lost contact with the facility showing a handful of specialized powered suits in inventory.  You are free to take any that are left."
msgstr ""
"During the Cataclysm, we lost contact with one of our sister sites, LIXA.  Aerial surveillance indicates that the facility's inhabitants are deceased, and beyond the now-zombified security detail, the site should be sparsely populated.  We want you to enter the facility and make a copy of what they were researching on the provided thumb drive.  Additionally, we will be providing you with a keycard that should at the very least get you in the front door.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We're offering a standard 5 HGC for successful retrieval of the data.  If that isn't enough of an incentive, we do have a manifest from before we lost contact with the facility showing a handful of specialised powered suits in inventory.  You are free to take any that are left."

msgid "[6 HGC] I'd like to buy the rest of the armor set now."
msgstr "[6 HGC] I'd like to buy the rest of the armour set now."

msgid "I'd like to request a set of armor."
msgstr "I'd like to request a set of armour."

msgid "How is my ordered armor going?"
msgstr "How is my ordered armour going?"

msgid "I would like you to upgrade my modular defense system."
msgstr "I would like you to upgrade my modular defence system."

msgid "My RM13 combat armor has taken some damage.  Could someone repair it for me?"
msgstr "My RM13 combat armour has taken some damage.  Could someone repair it for me?"

msgid "How are my armor repairs coming?"
msgstr "How are my armour repairs coming?"

msgid "At the moment, no.  While you are no doubt proficient, distribution of prototype equipment is so far restricted to trusted field agents.  Were someone else from the organization to vouch for your competency, we may consider extending access."
msgstr "At the moment, no.  While you are no doubt proficient, distribution of prototype equipment is so far restricted to trusted field agents.  Were someone else from the organisation to vouch for your competency, we may consider extending access."

msgid "Yes, Foster gave you quite a recommendation.  Very well - I will authorize you access to our prototype fabrication services for agents in the field.  This includes the Hybrid Weapons Platform, alongside the ability to order spare or replacement parts for your field gear."
msgstr "Yes, Foster gave you quite a recommendation.  Very well - I will authorise you access to our prototype fabrication services for agents in the field.  This includes the Hybrid Weapons Platform, alongside the ability to order spare or replacement parts for your field gear."

msgid ""
"The Platform is complete.  As a reminder, the HWP will not function as a weapon without a conversion kit installed.  Transferring the requested items now.\"\n"
"\n"
"The tray shakes as several heavy objects are dropped into it, and it slides open.  Inside: the Hybrid Weapons Platform.  On its own, it doesn't look like much; it resembles the body of a service rifle without a stock or barrel, colored in sleek black with blue highlights around the magazine well.  Small yellow arrows and inscriptions are present at certain points, highlighting the fasteners used to assemble the thing in earnest.  Accompanying the Platform itself is a series of four bundles of parts for it, each held together using velcro strips and tagged by caliber.  A drawstring nylon bag, embroidered with the Hub's logo and filled with proprietary tools, completes the whole package.\n"
"\n"
"All in all, not a bad deal.\n"
"\n"
"\"Should you require magazines of any given caliber, we are willing to provide them through standard requisitions.  We hope you find its performance to be satisfactory."
msgstr ""
"The Platform is complete.  As a reminder, the HWP will not function as a weapon without a conversion kit installed.  Transferring the requested items now.\"\n"
"\n"
"The tray shakes as several heavy objects are dropped into it, and it slides open.  Inside: the Hybrid Weapons Platform.  On its own, it doesn't look like much; it resembles the body of a service rifle without a stock or barrel, coloured in sleek black with blue highlights around the magazine well.  Small yellow arrows and inscriptions are present at certain points, highlighting the fasteners used to assemble the thing in earnest.  Accompanying the Platform itself is a series of four bundles of parts for it, each held together using velcro strips and tagged by calibre.  A drawstring nylon bag, embroidered with the Hub's logo and filled with proprietary tools, completes the whole package.\n"
"\n"
"All in all, not a bad deal.\n"
"\n"
"\"Should you require magazines of any given calibre, we are willing to provide them through standard requisitions.  We hope you find its performance to be satisfactory."

msgid ""
"I'll spare you the marketing pitch.  The Hybrid Weapons Platform - or more commonly the HWP - is a weapons platform capable of supporting multiple calibers via the use of quick-release adapters.  On its own, the platform does nothing; each adapter, however, allows it to chamber and fire a different type of round.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Each new HWP is printed to order.  Materials will require eight HGC up front, and fabrication will take seven days."
msgstr ""
"I'll spare you the marketing pitch.  The Hybrid Weapons Platform - or more commonly the HWP - is a weapons platform capable of supporting multiple calibres via the use of quick-release adaptors.  On its own, the platform does nothing; each adaptor, however, allows it to chamber and fire a different type of round.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Each new HWP is printed to order.  Materials will require eight HGC up front, and fabrication will take seven days."

msgid "Tell me about the adapters.  Does it come with any?"
msgstr "Tell me about the adaptors.  Does it come with any?"

msgid "Adapters are standalone conversion kits, and can be swapped in the field without any tools, though it will take a minute or so.  The factory standard includes adapters for the following calibers… 5.56 NATO, 7.62 NATO, 9mm Parabellum, and 12-gauge shotshell.  Two loaded magazines are also provided for each of these calibers, and additional empty magazines can be purchased through trade.  A maintenance kit with the necessary tools to service the Platform is also provided."
msgstr "Adaptors are standalone conversion kits, and can be swapped in the field without any tools, though it will take a minute or so.  The factory standard includes adaptors for the following calibres… 5.56 NATO, 7.62 NATO, 9mm Parabellum, and 12-gauge shotshell.  Two loaded magazines are also provided for each of these calibres, and additional empty magazines can be purchased through trade.  A maintenance kit with the necessary tools to service the Platform is also provided."

msgid ""
"Yes we have!  The disk contained the configuration necessary to print our armors with a much more resilient composite than was previously available to us, without sacrificing any maneuverability.  As a form of payment, we are willing to provide you with the first functional models of the armor at a good price - six HGC.  While that may seem steep, the materials used are very high-end, and six coins just barely covers the production cost alone.  If you are unwilling or incapable of filling that price now, the offer will remain available indefinitely - just let us know when you'd like it.\n"
"\n"
"\"Should you find anything else of interest in the world, please bring it to us.  We would be happy to collaborate like this again in the future."
msgstr ""
"Yes we have!  The disk contained the configuration necessary to print our armours with a much more resilient composite than was previously available to us, without sacrificing any manoeuvrability.  As a form of payment, we are willing to provide you with the first functional models of the armour at a good price - six HGC.  While that may seem steep, the materials used are very high-end, and six coins just barely covers the production cost alone.  If you are unwilling or incapable of filling that price now, the offer will remain available indefinitely - just let us know when you'd like it.\n"
"\n"
"\"Should you find anything else of interest in the world, please bring it to us.  We would be happy to collaborate like this again in the future."

msgid "[6 HGC] Let's see what this armor is capable of."
msgstr "[6 HGC] Let's see what this armour is capable of."

msgid "Understood.  The parts will finish fabrication in 24 hours, once you hand over the stipulated HGC.  Depending on our currently available selection, the price will range from 2 to 4 HGC for non-specialty equipment."
msgstr "Understood.  The parts will finish fabrication in 24 hours, once you hand over the stipulated HGC.  Depending on our currently available selection, the price will range from 2 to 4 HGC for non-speciality equipment."

msgid "[3 HGC] I'd like to request a replacement Modular Defense System."
msgstr "[3 HGC] I'd like to request a replacement Modular Defence System."

msgid "[2 HGC] I'd like to request a set of prototype armor."
msgstr "[2 HGC] I'd like to request a set of prototype armour."

msgid "[4 HGC] I'd like to request a set of turnout armor."
msgstr "[4 HGC] I'd like to request a set of turnout armour."

msgid "[4 HGC] I'd like to request a set of ballistic armor."
msgstr "[4 HGC] I'd like to request a set of ballistic armour."

msgid "[4 HGC] I'd like to request a set of kinetic armor."
msgstr "[4 HGC] I'd like to request a set of kinetic armour."

msgid "[12 HGC] I'd like to request a set of soldier armor."
msgstr "[12 HGC] I'd like to request a set of soldier armour."

msgid "Yes, we've finished printing the requested armor pieces.  Transferring to you now."
msgstr "Yes, we've finished printing the requested armour pieces.  Transferring to you now."

msgid "&The camera starts scanning the armor, after a moment the intercom cracks back to life.  \"This technology is currently not within our database, we can probably repair it but we'll need to reverse-engineer it first.  We estimate the repairs to take around a month and a half, and they'll have an increased fee of 12 coins.  Please make sure everything has been removed from the suit before giving it to us.\""
msgstr "&The camera starts scanning the armour, after a moment the intercom cracks back to life.  \"This technology is currently not within our database, we can probably repair it but we'll need to reverse-engineer it first.  We estimate the repairs to take around a month and a half, and they'll have an increased fee of 12 coins.  Please make sure everything has been removed from the suit before giving it to us.\""

msgid "Yes, that is within our capabilities.  For ten coins, repairs and adjustments can be completed by tomorrow; we will recharge the internal battery as well.  Please note that if you have made any modifications to the armor, it will be reverted to factory standard as part of the repairs."
msgstr "Yes, that is within our capabilities.  For ten coins, repairs and adjustments can be completed by tomorrow; we will recharge the internal battery as well.  Please note that if you have made any modifications to the armour, it will be reverted to factory standard as part of the repairs."

msgid ""
"We've made some notable progress.  The anchor itself appears to provide some degree of protection from extradimensional phenomena, and we believe that we can integrate it into our current modular armor system.  This will, however, make it heavier and less portable.  The armor will remain wearable outside of metal armor, although it will be a more snug fit than the anchor alone would have been.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We are returning the anchor now."
msgstr ""
"We've made some notable progress.  The anchor itself appears to provide some degree of protection from extradimensional phenomena, and we believe that we can integrate it into our current modular armour system.  This will, however, make it heavier and less portable.  The armour will remain wearable outside of metal armour, although it will be a more snug fit than the anchor alone would have been.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We are returning the anchor now."

msgid "Very well; we will need one coin for materials costs, as well as the anchor itself and the modular defense system you wish to combine it with.  As usual, I encourage you to remove everything from the pockets before handing them over for processing.  We'll need one day for construction and one day to verify efficacy."
msgstr "Very well; we will need one coin for materials costs, as well as the anchor itself and the modular defence system you wish to combine it with.  As usual, I encourage you to remove everything from the pockets before handing them over for processing.  We'll need one day for construction and one day to verify efficacy."

msgid ""
"What the gas mask does should be obvious; we'll provide you with a cartridge, of course.  The environment suit is full-body, and protects you from water, harmful radiation, and environmental hazards.  It's also rated to protect from electric shocks of up to twelve thousand volts.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Bear in mind that the suit isn't armor.  It will keep you safe from the environment, but it's just Nomex and it won't protect you from anything stronger than a punch.  The modular defense system is designed to fit over it, so I'd urge you to bring them both if fighting is unavoidable."
msgstr ""
"What the gas mask does should be obvious; we'll provide you with a cartridge, of course.  The environment suit is full-body, and protects you from water, harmful radiation, and environmental hazards.  It's also rated to protect from electric shocks of up to twelve thousand volts.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Bear in mind that the suit isn't armour.  It will keep you safe from the environment, but it's just Nomex and it won't protect you from anything stronger than a punch.  The modular defence system is designed to fit over it, so I'd urge you to bring them both if fighting is unavoidable."

msgid "Since business is increasing around here, I've decided to start selling more specialized metal.  Problem is, I can't separate the metal out.  Fortunately, I found some old schematics on a machine for this sort of thing.  If you could get me 25 magnetrons, I can melt down the sorted stuff into bars.  I can quickly pay you in raw materials."
msgstr "Since business is increasing around here, I've decided to start selling more specialised metal.  Problem is, I can't separate the metal out.  Fortunately, I found some old schematics on a machine for this sort of thing.  If you could get me 25 magnetrons, I can melt down the sorted stuff into bars.  I can quickly pay you in raw materials."

msgid "Establish trade relations between the scrapper and a refugee center, and bring back a writ of the agreement."
msgstr "Establish trade relations between the scrapper and a refugee centre, and bring back a writ of the agreement."

msgid "I was out scavenging recently, and I found one of those old evac shelters.  Turns out the computer was still on and had an address for a refugee center.  I figure they might want some spare metal, so I need you to go over there and strike a deal with them."
msgstr "I was out scavenging recently, and I found one of those old evac shelters.  Turns out the computer was still on and had an address for a refugee centre.  I figure they might want some spare metal, so I need you to go over there and strike a deal with them."

msgid "Business has been booming since you made a deal with that refugee center.  The last caravan that came by here mentioned something about a blacksmith down some old road.  Sounds like another business opportunity, so I need you to go over there and make a deal."
msgstr "Business has been booming since you made a deal with that refugee centre.  The last caravan that came by here mentioned something about a blacksmith down some old road.  Sounds like another business opportunity, so I need you to go over there and make a deal."

msgid "asshole"
msgstr "arsehole"

msgctxt "<name_b>"
msgid "dumpster"
msgstr "skip"

msgid "fellow traveler"
msgstr "fellow traveller"

msgid "I miss the cozy warmth of a fireplace in winter."
msgstr "I miss the cosy warmth of a fireplace in winter."

msgid "Heard any good rumors?"
msgstr "Heard any good rumours?"

msgid "I wonder if we'll ever see real civilization again, or if this is just the new normal."
msgstr "I wonder if we'll ever see real civilisation again, or if this is just the new normal."

msgid "I've heard rumors about entire towns just vanishing overnight.  No bodies, no signs of struggle.  Creepy, huh?"
msgstr "I've heard rumours about entire towns just vanishing overnight.  No bodies, no signs of struggle.  Creepy, huh?"

msgid "When do you think you realized the world was ending?  For me, it was that damned YouTube video with the lady killing the baby.  Holy shit, you know?"
msgstr "When do you think you realised the world was ending?  For me, it was that damned YouTube video with the lady killing the baby.  Holy shit, you know?"

msgid "You think there's a chance this was all just one big mistake?  Some accident that spiraled out of control?"
msgstr "You think there's a chance this was all just one big mistake?  Some accident that spiralled out of control?"

msgid "I read somewhere that human behavior changes in the presence of certain frequencies.  What if someone was broadcasting those right before the Cataclysm?"
msgstr "I read somewhere that human behaviour changes in the presence of certain frequencies.  What if someone was broadcasting those right before the Cataclysm?"

msgid "So many parts of this still don't fit together.  Who created the zombies?  What powers them?  Maybe the rumors of mind control drugs were true all along, and someone found a way to bioengineer living dead."
msgstr "So many parts of this still don't fit together.  Who created the zombies?  What powers them?  Maybe the rumours of mind control drugs were true all along, and someone found a way to bioengineer living dead."

msgid "I miss fresh fruit.  There's something about biting into a juicy apple that canned stuff just can't replicate."
msgstr "I miss fresh fruit.  There's something about biting into a juicy apple that tinned stuff just can't replicate."

msgid "You know what I miss?  Movie theaters.  You think Hollywood survived this?  Maybe there's a bunch of zombie actors out there, filmin' shit out of reflex.  Hah, I'd watch that shit."
msgstr "You know what I miss?  Movie theatres.  You think Hollywood survived this?  Maybe there's a bunch of zombie actors out there, filmin' shit out of reflex.  Hah, I'd watch that shit."

msgid "I don't know about you, but I'm gonna savor this moment of peace."
msgstr "I don't know about you, but I'm gonna savour this moment of peace."

msgid "Better grab your <freaking> pants, we're facing a"
msgstr "Better grab your <freaking> trousers, we're facing a"

msgid "Wake up, something's up.  Bet it's some assholes causing trouble."
msgstr "Wake up, something's up.  Bet it's some arseholes causing trouble."

msgid "I feel like I'm shriveling up."
msgstr "I feel like I'm shrivelling up."

msgid "Feels like I'm baptizing my insides."
msgstr "Feels like I'm baptising my insides."

msgid "Eating good in the post-apocalyptic neighborhood."
msgstr "Eating good in the post-apocalyptic neighbourhood."

msgid "Not bad for canned food."
msgstr "Not bad for tinned food."

msgid "Uhm, <name_g>, I don't mean to criticize, but we should focus on distributing some food into the basecamp larder."
msgstr "Uhm, <name_g>, I don't mean to criticise, but we should focus on distributing some food into the basecamp larder."

#, no-c-format
msgid "<mypronoun> will reserve 100% of CBM power for defense or utility CBMs."
msgstr "<mypronoun> will reserve 100% of CBM power for defence or utility CBMs."

#, no-c-format
msgid "<mypronoun> will reserve 75% of CBM power for defense or utility CBMs."
msgstr "<mypronoun> will reserve 75% of CBM power for defence or utility CBMs."

#, no-c-format
msgid "<mypronoun> will reserve 50% of CBM power for defense or utility CBMs."
msgstr "<mypronoun> will reserve 50% of CBM power for defence or utility CBMs."

#, no-c-format
msgid "<mypronoun> will reserve 25% of CBM power for defense or utility CBMs."
msgstr "<mypronoun> will reserve 25% of CBM power for defence or utility CBMs."

msgid "<mypronoun> will not reserve any power for defense or utility CBMs."
msgstr "<mypronoun> will not reserve any power for defence or utility CBMs."

msgid "I'm a lone traveler, <name_g>."
msgstr "I'm a lone traveller, <name_g>."

msgid "I love trying new strains and flavors."
msgstr "I love trying new strains and flavours."

msgid "Pass the weed, asshole."
msgstr "Pass the weed, arsehole."

msgid "Weed is my favorite way to chill out."
msgstr "Weed is my favourite way to chill out."

msgid "A neighbor of mine got addicted to weed, lost his home and job."
msgstr "A neighbour of mine got addicted to weed, lost his home and job."

msgid "I used to smoke weed every day, but I realized it was just holding me back."
msgstr "I used to smoke weed every day, but I realised it was just holding me back."

msgid "Spiraling spirals."
msgstr "Spiralling spirals."

msgid "Thorazine will cloud your judgment."
msgstr "Thorazine will cloud your judgement."

msgid "Can I interest you in a trim?  It'll cost you 6 merch for a haircut or 3 for a beard trim.  I can do color and styling too."
msgstr "Can I interest you in a trim?  It'll cost you 6 merch for a haircut or 3 for a beard trim.  I can do colour and styling too."

msgid "The doctor needs some help building an anesthetic machine.  Do you have anything that could help?"
msgstr "The doctor needs some help building an anaesthetic machine.  Do you have anything that could help?"

msgid "We have a policy of keeping information to ourselves.  Ask the patrons if you want to hear rumors or news."
msgstr "We have a policy of keeping information to ourselves.  Ask the patrons if you want to hear rumours or news."

msgid "Sugar and molasses remains in short supply.  I've put in a request for more, but it is unlikely that I'm going to see a reliable source for some time.  If you are interested, we are going to need sugar beet seeds to meet future demand regardless of what the scavengers can find.  Could you bring me at least enough seeds to plant a small 10 meter long patch?"
msgstr "Sugar and molasses remains in short supply.  I've put in a request for more, but it is unlikely that I'm going to see a reliable source for some time.  If you are interested, we are going to need sugar beet seeds to meet future demand regardless of what the scavengers can find.  Could you bring me at least enough seeds to plant a small 10 metre long patch?"

msgid "Find 12 60-Liter Metal Tanks"
msgstr "Find 12 60-Litre Metal Tanks"

msgid "The drinks we brew here have become a major draw for visitors and the occasional trader.  Our batches have become larger, but we are still running out of storage space between trading runs.  I've been able to get a few volunteers to help me build a set of standing tanks, but I still need 12 60-liter metal tanks to build them.  I've talked with the scrappers, but we are a low priority at the moment."
msgstr "The drinks we brew here have become a major draw for visitors and the occasional trader.  Our batches have become larger, but we are still running out of storage space between trading runs.  I've been able to get a few volunteers to help me build a set of standing tanks, but I still need 12 60-litre metal tanks to build them.  I've talked with the scrappers, but we are a low priority at the moment."

msgid "Do you have the 60-liter metal tanks?"
msgstr "Do you have the 60-litre metal tanks?"

msgid "Find 2 200-Liter Drums"
msgstr "Find 2 200-Litre Drums"

msgid "The other survivor outposts that we have contact with have been more than eager to trade for beer or other drinks.  Transporting the drinks to them has presented a number of challenges though.  If you could locate a pair of 200-liter drums, we should be able to keep them supplied while turning a significant profit."
msgstr "The other survivor outposts that we have contact with have been more than eager to trade for beer or other drinks.  Transporting the drinks to them has presented a number of challenges though.  If you could locate a pair of 200-litre drums, we should be able to keep them supplied while turning a significant profit."

msgid "Do you have the 200-liter drums?"
msgstr "Do you have the 200-litre drums?"

msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid "I was among one of the first groups of immigrants sent here to fortify the outpost.  I might have exaggerated my construction skills to get the hell out of the refugee center.  Unless you are a trader, there isn't much work there and food was really becoming scarce when I left."
msgstr "I was among one of the first groups of immigrants sent here to fortify the outpost.  I might have exaggerated my construction skills to get the hell out of the refugee centre.  Unless you are a trader, there isn't much work there and food was really becoming scarce when I left."

