msgid "The tank of the Super Soldier project.  You are one of a few augmented soldiers to be used as a heavy support to infantry.  With ranged, armor and regenerative capabilities, you can endure heavy damage and return it in kind."
msgstr "The tank of the Super Soldier project.  You are one of a few augmented soldiers to be used as a heavy support to infantry.  With ranged, armour and regenerative capabilities, you can endure heavy damage and return it in kind."

msgid "Makeshift Command Center"
msgstr "Makeshift Command Centre"

msgid "The ultimate bionic mutant.  Only God knows why it exists.  With incredible power, armor and bionics on its side, victory won't come easy."
msgstr "The ultimate bionic mutant.  Only God knows why it exists.  With incredible power, armour and bionics on its side, victory won't come easy."

msgid "An advanced, well-equipped member of the military that still succumbed to the cataclysm.  This one is relatively well-armored, wielding some sort of LMG as though it recalls how to use it."
msgstr "An advanced, well-equipped member of the military that still succumbed to the cataclysm.  This one is relatively well-armoured, wielding some sort of LMG as though it recalls how to use it."

msgid "An advanced, well-equipped member of the military that still succumbed to the cataclysm.  This one is relatively well-armored, and the anti-tank weapon it's carrying looks to be in working order.  Run."
msgstr "An advanced, well-equipped member of the military that still succumbed to the cataclysm.  This one is relatively well-armoured, and the anti-tank weapon it's carrying looks to be in working order.  Run."

msgid "An advanced, well-equipped member of the military that still succumbed to the cataclysm.  This one has no sign of its signature weaponry and its armor is in tatters, yet it still marches on with unnerving confidence and speed."
msgstr "An advanced, well-equipped member of the military that still succumbed to the cataclysm.  This one has no sign of its signature weaponry and its armour is in tatters, yet it still marches on with unnerving confidence and speed."

msgid "Natural Armor"
msgstr "Natural Armour"

msgid "You start with the Bionic Combatives style.  A modern combat style for the post-modern human.  Nicknamed \"Biojutsu\", Bionic Combatives combines integrated weaponry, armor and augments into an consolidated fighting discipline."
msgstr "You start with the Bionic Combatives style.  A modern combat style for the post-modern human.  Nicknamed \"Biojutsu\", Bionic Combatives combines integrated weaponry, armour and augments into an consolidated fighting discipline."

msgid "You don't recognize this aug configuration, Hunter?"
msgstr "You don't recognise this aug configuration, Hunter?"

msgid "You're kidding, right?  You really don't know?  Is that badge actually yours…? Maybe that mindwipe rumor was true after all…"
msgstr "You're kidding, right?  You really don't know?  Is that badge actually yours…? Maybe that mindwipe rumour was true after all…"

msgid "I'm trying to reach a hideout built by former scientists who worked on the Bio-Weapon Project.  Rumor has it they live somewhere in the woods.  Maybe you could help me find it…"
msgstr "I'm trying to reach a hideout built by former scientists who worked on the Bio-Weapon Project.  Rumour has it they live somewhere in the woods.  Maybe you could help me find it…"

msgid "Used to be an old lab bunker.  We had the lower level gutted and remodeled to make it livable.  Better than nothing at least."
msgstr "Used to be an old lab bunker.  We had the lower level gutted and remodelled to make it liveable.  Better than nothing at least."

msgid "They're the other team in the fucking death matches these assholes would stage for their amusement.  They're the ones that've been here long enough to actually get into it…"
msgstr "They're the other team in the fucking death matches these arseholes would stage for their amusement.  They're the ones that've been here long enough to actually get into it…"

msgid "Hey there!  Welcome to the Command Center."
msgstr "Hey there!  Welcome to the Command Centre."

msgid "If you can deliver effective fire with something high-caliber, or even explosive, you should have good odds of taking one out in a single shot.  Be prepared for the chance they might limp away from it though, these things are tougher than they look."
msgstr "If you can deliver effective fire with something high-calibre, or even explosive, you should have good odds of taking one out in a single shot.  Be prepared for the chance they might limp away from it though, these things are tougher than they look."

msgid "Ha!  You really have no idea, do you?  Have you ever fought an augmented abomination?  How about the ones that've succumbed to undeath?  Tough, right?  They have nothing on Apophis.  It's incredibly durable thanks to its armor and its heavy weaponry is a step above the rest of the Project.  Apophis is far more dangerous than any ordinary enemy."
msgstr "Ha!  You really have no idea, do you?  Have you ever fought an augmented abomination?  How about the ones that've succumbed to undeath?  Tough, right?  They have nothing on Apophis.  It's incredibly durable thanks to its armour and its heavy weaponry is a step above the rest of the Project.  Apophis is far more dangerous than any ordinary enemy."

msgid "No.  Place was fairly quiet initially, no sign of those things when we arrived.  We went in to make sure it was clear, then the guy I was traveling with kept watch outside.  Was maybe a day or two of turning the place inside-out when a group of them swarmed the area, tore the poor bastard apart.  I think he took a few with him, but even they aren't all immune to this zombie thing.  I holed up in the bunker once I realized I was alone…"
msgstr "No.  Place was fairly quiet initially, no sign of those things when we arrived.  We went in to make sure it was clear, then the guy I was travelling with kept watch outside.  Was maybe a day or two of turning the place inside-out when a group of them swarmed the area, tore the poor bastard apart.  I think he took a few with him, but even they aren't all immune to this zombie thing.  I holed up in the bunker once I realised I was alone…"

msgid "Command Center Members"
msgstr "Command Centre Members"

msgid "Members of the Command Center seeking refuge from …something.  They have intel and some connections to the Old Guard."
msgstr "Members of the Command Centre seeking refuge from …something.  They have intel and some connections to the Old Guard."

msgid "Ragtag branch of the military that survived the initial cataclysm.  Allied to the command center, they seek leadership in this new world."
msgstr "Ragtag branch of the military that survived the initial cataclysm.  Allied to the command centre, they seek leadership in this new world."

msgid "Creations of an unknown project with links to the cataclysm.  Allied to the command center since they are their creation."
msgstr "Creations of an unknown project with links to the cataclysm.  Allied to the command centre since they are their creation."

msgid "Get some decent armor and weapons, this fight won't be easy.  Assemble a team to make it easier.  Ask Lambda and Sigma if they want to join you, if you want.  A single person can't take it on…"
msgstr "Get some decent armour and weapons, this fight won't be easy.  Assemble a team to make it easier.  Ask Lambda and Sigma if they want to join you, if you want.  A single person can't take it on…"

msgid "Reach Command Center"
msgstr "Reach Command Centre"

msgid "Center Leader"
msgstr "Centre Leader"

msgid "survivor's armored scout suit"
msgid_plural "survivor's armored scout suits"
msgstr[0] "survivor's armoured scout suit"
msgstr[1] "survivor's armoured scout suits"

msgid "survivor plate armor"
msgid_plural "survivor plate armors"
msgstr[0] "survivor plate armour"
msgstr[1] "survivor plate armours"

msgid "A suit of Gothic plate armor modified with kevlar and leather, altered to better protect the gaps between plates and provide better protection from the elements."
msgstr "A suit of Gothic plate armour modified with kevlar and leather, altered to better protect the gaps between plates and provide better protection from the elements."

msgid "pair of survivor armored gauntlets"
msgid_plural "pairs of survivor armored gauntlets"
msgstr[0] "pair of survivor armoured gauntlets"
msgstr[1] "pairs of survivor armoured gauntlets"

msgid "pair of survivor armored boots"
msgid_plural "pairs of survivor armored boots"
msgstr[0] "pair of survivor armoured boots"
msgstr[1] "pairs of survivor armoured boots"

msgid "A heavy set of armor plated boots, modified with kevlar to better protect from the elements."
msgstr "A heavy set of armour plated boots, modified with kevlar to better protect from the elements."

msgid "light sentinel armor"
msgid_plural "light sentinel armor"
msgstr[0] "light sentinel armour"
msgstr[1] "light sentinel armour"

msgid "A fairly light full-body suit of gray ballistic armor, one size fits most, with separate helmet.  Made from a fabric bodysuit with advanced composite plates, it is relatively easy to move in but protection is minimal, only rated for pistol-caliber rounds and fragmentation.  It also has two adjustable pouches for various sizes of magazines."
msgstr "A fairly light full-body suit of grey ballistic armour, one size fits most, with separate helmet.  Made from a fabric bodysuit with advanced composite plates, it is relatively easy to move in but protection is minimal, only rated for pistol-calibre rounds and fragmentation.  It also has two adjustable pouches for various sizes of magazines."

msgid "sentinel armor"
msgid_plural "sentinel armor"
msgstr[0] "sentinel armour"
msgstr[1] "sentinel armour"

msgid "A full-body suit of gray ballistic armor, one size fits most, with separate helmet.  Made with leather lining and advanced composite plates, it provides adequate protection against anything up to intermediate caliber ammunition, but may fail against full-power rifle rounds.  It also has two adjustable pouches for various sizes of magazines."
msgstr "A full-body suit of grey ballistic armour, one size fits most, with separate helmet.  Made with leather lining and advanced composite plates, it provides adequate protection against anything up to intermediate calibre ammunition, but may fail against full-power rifle rounds.  It also has two adjustable pouches for various sizes of magazines."

msgid "heavy sentinel armor"
msgid_plural "heavy sentinel armor"
msgstr[0] "heavy sentinel armour"
msgstr[1] "heavy sentinel armour"

msgid "A heavy-duty full-body suit of gray ballistic armor, one size fits most, with separate helmet.  Made from heavy-duty lining with advanced plating, it protects the body rather well against most rifle rounds, but may be too cumbersome for most situations.  It also has two adjustable pouches for various sizes of magazines."
msgstr "A heavy-duty full-body suit of grey ballistic armour, one size fits most, with separate helmet.  Made from heavy-duty lining with advanced plating, it protects the body rather well against most rifle rounds, but may be too cumbersome for most situations.  It also has two adjustable pouches for various sizes of magazines."

msgid "A fairly light full-face ballistic helmet, one size fits most.  Made from a fabric lining with advanced composite plates, it is only rated for pistol-caliber rounds and fragmentation."
msgstr "A fairly light full-face ballistic helmet, one size fits most.  Made from a fabric lining with advanced composite plates, it is only rated for pistol-calibre rounds and fragmentation."

msgid "A full-face ballistic helmet, one size fits most.  Made with leather lining and advanced composite plates, it provides adequate protection against anything up to intermediate caliber ammunition."
msgstr "A full-face ballistic helmet, one size fits most.  Made with leather lining and advanced composite plates, it provides adequate protection against anything up to intermediate calibre ammunition."

msgid "Carapace Armor Cooling"
msgstr "Carapace Armour Cooling"

msgid "This is used to make salvaged carapace armor provide further cooling if overheating."
msgstr "This is used to make salvaged carapace armour provide further cooling if overheating."

msgid "salvaged carapace armor"
msgid_plural "salvaged carapace armors"
msgstr[0] "salvaged carapace armour"
msgstr[1] "salvaged carapace armours"

msgid "A second skin of alien sinew and steel support, covered in armor plates made of resin.  Salvaged using pre-cataclysm research into other living weaponry, it's been practically mutilated to fit a human (or mutant) wearer.  Activating it will reduce the suit's encumbrance, make your attacks faster, enhance strength and dexterity, protect the wearer from toxic gas, serve as a rebreather, enhance stamina and carry capacity, and provide some protection from outside temperature.  Recharges in sunlight, being active will also gradually fatigue the user and affect healthiness, plus render them more vulnerable to electric shocks."
msgstr "A second skin of alien sinew and steel support, covered in armour plates made of resin.  Salvaged using pre-cataclysm research into other living weaponry, it's been practically mutilated to fit a human (or mutant) wearer.  Activating it will reduce the suit's encumbrance, make your attacks faster, enhance strength and dexterity, protect the wearer from toxic gas, serve as a rebreather, enhance stamina and carry capacity, and provide some protection from outside temperature.  Recharges in sunlight, being active will also gradually fatigue the user and affect healthiness, plus render them more vulnerable to electric shocks."

msgid "salvaged carapace armor (on)"
msgid_plural "salvaged carapace armors (on)"
msgstr[0] "salvaged carapace armour (on)"
msgstr[1] "salvaged carapace armours (on)"

msgid "A second skin of alien sinew and steel support, covered in armor plates made of resin.  Salvaged using pre-cataclysm research into other living weaponry, it's been practically mutilated to fit a human (or mutant) wearer.  Currently active, it enhances strength and dexterity, make your attacks faster, protects the wearer from toxic gas, serves as a rebreather, enhances stamina and carry capacity, and provides some protection from outside temperature.  Recharges in sunlight, being active also gradually fatigues the user and affects healthiness, plus renders them more vulnerable to electric shocks."
msgstr "A second skin of alien sinew and steel support, covered in armour plates made of resin.  Salvaged using pre-cataclysm research into other living weaponry, it's been practically mutilated to fit a human (or mutant) wearer.  Currently active, it enhances strength and dexterity, make your attacks faster, protects the wearer from toxic gas, serves as a rebreather, enhances stamina and carry capacity, and provides some protection from outside temperature.  Recharges in sunlight, being active also gradually fatigues the user and affects healthiness, plus renders them more vulnerable to electric shocks."

msgid "The exo-wings whir to life, becoming a fluttering blur of green and gray."
msgstr "The exo-wings whirr to life, becoming a fluttering blur of green and grey."

msgid "makeshift hydraulic armor Noise"
msgstr "makeshift hydraulic armour Noise"

msgid "This is used to make the player a lot less stealthy, but also punch harder on top of the armor's strength bonus."
msgstr "This is used to make the player a lot less stealthy, but also punch harder on top of the armour's strength bonus."

msgid "makeshift hydraulic armor"
msgid_plural "makeshift hydraulic armors"
msgstr[0] "makeshift hydraulic armour"
msgstr[1] "makeshift hydraulic armours"

msgid "Your armor sputters but fails to start up."
msgstr "Your armour sputters but fails to start up."

msgid "Your makeshift hydraulic armor roars to life, servos kicking into gear!"
msgstr "Your makeshift hydraulic armour roars to life, servos kicking into gear!"

msgid "makeshift hydraulic armor (on)"
msgid_plural "makeshift hydraulic armors (on)"
msgstr[0] "makeshift hydraulic armour (on)"
msgstr[1] "makeshift hydraulic armours (on)"

msgid "An incredibly heavy suit of steel and kevlar plates covering a network of hydraulics, driven by pieces of a stripped-down diesel engine jury-rigged to assist the wearer's movements.  It's currently active, strengthening the wearer, increasing raw speed and making the armor less encumbering, but also being warmer and making stealth more difficult."
msgstr "An incredibly heavy suit of steel and kevlar plates covering a network of hydraulics, driven by pieces of a stripped-down diesel engine jury-rigged to assist the wearer's movements.  It's currently active, strengthening the wearer, increasing raw speed and making the armour less encumbering, but also being warmer and making stealth more difficult."

msgid "You shut the makeshift hydraulic armor off."
msgstr "You shut the makeshift hydraulic armour off."

msgid "Your makeshift hydraulic armor sputters and dies!"
msgstr "Your makeshift hydraulic armour sputters and dies!"

msgid "Your armor whirs with activity."
msgstr "Your armour whirrs with activity."

msgid "Your armor's engine floods and cuts out!"
msgstr "Your armour's engine floods and cuts out!"

msgid "This implant provides an experimental military hydrogen cell, able to produce large spikes of power for intense usage.  Its network of pressurized storage has two chambers, one can hold 500 ml of hydrogen gas, the other 5 rounds of denser hydrogen canisters used in plasma weaponry.  The label advises not to use it in confined spaces, and to keep moving if used during a military operation, due to hazardous levels of waste heat."
msgstr "This implant provides an experimental military hydrogen cell, able to produce large spikes of power for intense usage.  Its network of pressurised storage has two chambers, one can hold 500 ml of hydrogen gas, the other 5 rounds of denser hydrogen canisters used in plasma weaponry.  The label advises not to use it in confined spaces, and to keep moving if used during a military operation, due to hazardous levels of waste heat."

msgid "Hazard Stabilizer System CBM"
msgid_plural "Hazard Stabilizer System CBMs"
msgstr[0] "Hazard Stabiliser System CBM"
msgstr[1] "Hazard Stabiliser System CBMs"

msgid "A network of specialized medical equipment, implanted just under the skin.  Activating it will induce temporary changes in body chemistry, providing immunity to acid and biological damage, and preventing exposure to contact toxins and venom."
msgstr "A network of specialised medical equipment, implanted just under the skin.  Activating it will induce temporary changes in body chemistry, providing immunity to acid and biological damage, and preventing exposure to contact toxins and venom."

msgid "Hazard Stabilizer System"
msgstr "Hazard Stabiliser System"

msgid "Installed throughout your body, just under the skin, is a network of specialized medical equipment.  When activated, it will synthesize antitoxins and catalyze temporary chemical reactions in the muscles and skin.  While active, you will be immune to acid and biological damage, keeping the body relatively stable even if severely poisoned.  It will also prevent, but not cure, the effects of contact and injected hazards, such as venom.  Food poisoning and toxic gas will still affect you, but you will not take damage-over-time from them."
msgstr "Installed throughout your body, just under the skin, is a network of specialised medical equipment.  When activated, it will synthesise antitoxins and catalyse temporary chemical reactions in the muscles and skin.  While active, you will be immune to acid and biological damage, keeping the body relatively stable even if severely poisoned.  It will also prevent, but not cure, the effects of contact and injected hazards, such as venom.  Food poisoning and toxic gas will still affect you, but you will not take damage-over-time from them."

msgid "Hazard Stabilization"
msgstr "Hazard Stabilisation"

msgid "The mechanics volume of the Rebuilding Civilization encyclopedia.  This book contains everything from simple machines to the inner workings of submarine engines in extremely fine detail.  This book is so technical, longwinded and dry that even bookworms and fast readers would find it hard to read.  Literally any other book on the subject would be a more efficient way to learn but if the books you have are missing specific information then this is a good substitute until you find something better."
